{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_014J7N35hp6oZvtgGHdHrYYQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed imagined experimental results for all \"planned\" experiments in the experiment plan, assuming the \"best\" tier outcome. Let me carefully go through each planned experiment and generate realistic predictions with rationales.\n\nLet me review the existing data points to calibrate:\n\n**Existing NER (SciERC) results:**\n- pilot_003 (N=8, T=1.0, ft_001 model): rho_sj=0.3808, rho_fk=0.3362\n- pilot_004 (N=8, T=1.0, ft_002_v2): rho_sj=0.3825, rho_fk=0.2590\n\n\n- pilot_005 (N=8, T=0.7, ft_002_v2): rho_sj=0.3875, rho_fk=0.3211\n\n**Existing RE (SciERC) results:**\n- pilot_005: full rho_sj=0.2343, cond rho_sj=0.3716\n\n**Best tier ranges:**\n- ner_sj_rho_scierc: [0.39, 0.45]\n- ner_sj_rho_conll: [0.35, 0.45]\n- ner_sj_rho_wnut: [0.33, 0.42]\n- ner_logprob_rho: [0.2, 0.28]\n- ner_exact_match_rho: [0.15, 0.25]\n- ner_entity_voting_rho: [0.25, 0.33]\n- ner_sj_minus_logprob: [0.08, 0.2]\n- ner_sj_auroc: [0.7, 0.8]\n- ner_sj_tau: [0.28, 0.35]\n- bestofN_f1_gain_sj_over_greedy: [3.0, 6.0]\n- bestofN_f1_gain_sj_over_log: (range incomplete)\n\nI'm looking at the performance benchmarks across different NER metrics and datasets to establish what constitutes a good tier range for each metric. Looking at the performance metrics across these baseline approaches and planned experiments. The log-prob baseline achieves around 0.2-0.28 rho, while exact-match and entity voting fall in the 0.15-0.25 and 0.25-0.33 ranges respectively. I'm planning to expand the evaluation metrics to include AUROC, tau, and calibration scores, then run a series of NER experiments across different datasets like SciERC, CoNLL-2003, and WNUT-17 to validate the approach, along with diagnostic analyses for relation extraction and sensitivity testing across temperature settings. Now I'm laying out the core narrative: SJ consistently outperforms log-prob baselines on NER with substantial margins, maintains a clear ranking across methods, replicates across datasets, and shows model-agnostic behavior, while RE signals uniformly degrade. I'm setting concrete baseline numbers for log-prob and exact-match experiments to establish the comparison points. Now I'm looking at the performance metrics across the remaining experiments—LLaMA's rho_sj comes in around 0.38, while the best-of-N approach shows meaningful F1 gains over both greedy and logprob baselines. The metrics expansion results show solid AUROC and tau values. I'm about to compile these into a structured format, though I want to double-check some of the exp-001 calculations first, particularly how the sample size affected that rho_sj improvement.\n\nFor the logprob experiment, the core issue is that sequence-level confidence scores don't translate cleanly to entity-level quality—a model can be confident about a sequence while still missing entities or generating hallucinations, and logprob misses the signal that comes from multiple samples agreeing on specific entities. Exact-match is running into similar limitations where it's too strict for capturing meaningful agreement.\n\nEntity voting is more promising since it operates at the entity level, but it only counts frequency without considering the broader structural patterns that SJ captures. I'm now thinking through how to structure the full experimental writeup with the necessary tables and figures for each comparison, and I need to double-check my baseline numbers for the NER task.\n\nLooking at the SciERC data more carefully: with the pilot results showing rho around 0.39 for SJ, I'd expect the best-tier performance to land around 0.42 with N=16. For logprob as a baseline, I'm estimating rho around 0.24, which would give a clean difference of 0.18—well above the threshold I need. The intuition here is that sequence-level log-probability gets diluted across all the tokens in the output, including formatting and structural elements, so it doesn't isolate entity correctness as effectively.\n\nNow thinking through the other baselines: exact-match voting would be extremely noisy since stochastic sampling produces minor variations in span boundaries and entity counts, so I'd expect that around 0.20. Entity-level voting is more competitive at roughly 0.29 since it operates at the right granularity, but it misses the set-level coherence that SJ captures. This gives me the ranking: SJ at 0.42, FK at 0.33, entity voting at 0.29, logprob at 0.24, and exact-match at 0.20.\n\nFor relation extraction, the full RE task shows all signals performing poorly in the 0.2 to 0.3 range, which aligns with the compound error propagation hypothesis. I'm ready to write out the comprehensive YAML with all experiment rationales and metrics. I'll pull the SciERC NER baseline numbers from the pilot data—529 instances with SJ at 0.3875—and use logprob at 0.24 with AUROC 0.63, exact-match at 0.19.\n\nNow looking at the best-of-N selection results, there's a clear performance hierarchy where entity voting and FK selection both outperform greedy F1 around 0.695-0.70, with logprob selection at 0.69 and exact-match at 0.68.\n\nSJ selection reaches about 0.715 with N=16, which represents roughly a 4.8 percentage point improvement over greedy and 2.5 points over logprob. The oracle ceiling sits at 0.776. I need to reconcile this with the expected gains from the tier specification, which suggests SJ should deliver 3-6 points over greedy and 1.5-4 points over logprob—so the observed 4.8 and 2.5 point gains fall right in that expected range.\n\nNow I'm working through the full YAML configuration for all 15 experiments, starting with the baseline approaches and then moving through the NER variants across different datasets.\n\nFor the temperature sensitivity analysis, I'm comparing the pilot runs at T=0.7 versus T=1.0 to understand how sampling temperature affects performance, pulling from the existing pilot data to establish the baseline metrics. sj=0.3825, RE full rho_sj=0.2441\n- T=0.7 (pilot_005): NER rho_sj=0.3875, RE full rho_sj=0.2343\n\nSo T=0.7 is slightly better on NER but slightly worse on RE. In best tier, we'd expect T=0.7 to be clearly better for NER (the sampling diversity at T=1.0 adds noise rather than signal for entities, while T=0.7 gives enough diversity to differentiate without too much noise). For RE, both are bad.\n\nActually, wait - these are already existing data points. exp-005 analyzes pilot_004 and pilot_005 data. So the \"expected results\" are just the analysis of existing data plus the new baseline signals computed in exp-012/013.\n\nexp-005 will compare T=0.7 versus T=1.0 across all signals—SJ, FK, logprob, exact-match—to show how the temperature affects the signal-to-noise tradeoff. At lower temperatures, the model becomes more confident and logprob values compress, while higher temperatures introduce more variance that could either help or hurt discriminative power depending on whether that variance is signal or noise.\n\nI'm predicting logprob performs slightly better at T=1.0 due to increased spread, but SJ remains superior at T=0.7 where consistency-based signals benefit from less noise. Rather than overthinking the exact predictions, I should just write the YAML configuration and keep the tier ranges internally consistent.\n\nNow for exp-008, I need to confirm the RE results with N=16 and check where the full signal rho values fall within the best tier ranges.\n\nFor exp-009, I'm planning to stratify instances by greedy F1 buckets and independent features like sentence length and entity count, which should reveal that SJ shows an inverted-U pattern for NER—most discriminative on medium-difficulty cases—while for RE it only helps where the model has some baseline capability.\n\nFor exp-010, I'm setting up best-of-N selection curves across different N values to demonstrate that SJ consistently outperforms across all settings.\n\nFor exp-011, I'm testing cross-domain robustness by training on one domain and evaluating on another, expecting SJ to maintain its advantage though with smaller margins.\n\nNow I'm ready to structure the full YAML specification. I need to think through the key tables for each experiment—a main comparison matrix showing signal performance across datasets, AUROC and calibration metrics, best-of-N results, temperature sensitivity analysis, RE diagnostics, and cross-model comparisons. Let me organize these as structured table descriptions.\n\nLooking at the output format more carefully, I should keep tables as structured data while describing figures in prose. Now I'm finalizing the performance numbers across all experiments to ensure consistency. For SciERC NER with N=16 and T=0.7, I'm setting SJ at ρ=0.42 with τ=0.31 and AUROC=0.75, then scaling down the other methods proportionally—FK at 0.33/0.24/0.68, entity voting at 0.29/0.22/0.65, logprob at 0.24/0.18/0.63, and exact-match at 0.19/0.14/0.58.\n\nNow I'm compiling the results for CoNLL-2003 and WNUT-17 with N=8 and T=0.7, maintaining the same relative performance gaps between methods while adjusting the absolute values slightly downward to reflect the smaller ensemble size and different dataset characteristics. Now I'm looking at the conditional relation extraction results, which show notably stronger correlations than the full task—SJ and logprob both hitting around 0.30-0.39 for ρ. Moving to the best-of-N selection experiments on NER with N=16, SJ selection substantially outperforms the baselines, gaining 4.5 percentage points over greedy baseline with an F1 of 0.712, while FK and entity voting also show meaningful improvements of 3.1 and 2.8 points respectively.\n\nThe gaps between methods are all within expected ranges, so I'm confident in the consistency. Now I need to write out the full YAML configuration, and I'm also considering a leave-one-out variant of SJ for the next experiment that would exclude each sample from the SJ computation to address any potential circularity issues—I'd expect this to maintain strong performance around 0.40 correlation despite the reduced sample size.\n\nLooking at calibration metrics, SJ shows much better calibration than the baselines with an ECE around 0.08 compared to logprob's 0.15 and FK's 0.12. For temperature sensitivity, the data suggests T=0.7 outperforms T=1.0 across both methods—SJ gains a modest 0.5 percentage points on NER while FK improves substantially by 6.2 percentage points, and logprob also benefits from the lower temperature by producing more concentrated probability distributions.\n\nNow I'm checking what exp-004 adds beyond the existing component-wise analysis—it looks like the additional breakdown includes per-relation-type comparisons, bootstrap confidence intervals across all rho measurements, conditional threshold sensitivity analysis, and a comprehensive comparison of confidence metrics that goes deeper than the component-level view.\n\nFor the relation types in SciERC, I'm thinking about how simpler, more frequent patterns like Used-for might show stronger consistency signals compared to rarer or more complex ones like Evaluate-for. The threshold sensitivity piece is important too—testing across T=0.5, T=0.7, and T=0.9 shows whether the sweet spot at T=0.7 holds up or if it's just an artifact of the specific threshold choice.\n\nFor exp-009 on capability stratification, I'm planning to break down NER performance by greedy F1 scores to see how consistency varies across different model capability levels.\n\nNow looking at the stratification results: there's an inverted-U pattern in SJ correlation across F1 buckets, but it's not a limitation of SJ itself—it's because uncertainty only exists in the middle range where the model is partially capable. At the extremes (F1=0 or F1=1), there's nothing uncertain to measure. I'm also checking independent proxies like sentence length and entity count, which show that simpler contexts (shorter sentences, fewer entities) have higher SJ correlation while complexity degrades it.\n\nFor the OOD robustness experiment, I'm planning to train on WNUT-17 social media data and test on CoNLL-2003 news or SciERC science domains. Even with distribution shift reducing overall correlations, SJ should maintain its advantage over other signals—the preliminary numbers show SJ at ρ=0.33 compared to FK at 0.25 and logprob at 0.21. Now I need to finalize the YAML output and double-check the RE tier specifications.\n\nLooking at the RE results, I'm verifying that the full-dataset numbers align with the best tier constraints. The pilot data shows SJ performing at ρ=0.24 on the full RE set, which fits within the [0.2, 0.3] range, and the conditional variant reaches ρ=0.35-0.42 as expected.\n\nI'm noticing something about how logprob behaves on RE compared to SJ—when entity identification becomes unreliable due to compound errors, the structural advantage that makes SJ useful elsewhere gets undermined. Logprob, being internal to the model, might actually degrade in a similar way, which would explain why both signals suffer together rather than one compensating for the other.\n\nLet me set the RE full numbers to reflect this convergence: SJ at 0.24, logprob at 0.23, entity voting at 0.21, FK at 0.19, and exact match at 0.13. This tells the story I'm after—on NER, SJ clearly outperforms logprob because of its structural sensitivity, but on RE, compound errors flatten everything out so the signals cluster together with no meaningful separation.\n\nFor the N=16 case with more samples, I'd expect modest improvement on RE full, pushing SJ up slightly to around 0.27, while the conditional performance would improve more noticeably.\n\nNow I need to write the output. I'm planning to include structured result tables and organize the YAML clearly. I should also verify the seed-level analysis for exp-001, checking the three seeds across N=16 to confirm the rho_sj values.\n\nGenerating YAML output...\n\nLooking at the calibration analysis more carefully for exp-015. For SJ, the confidence scores align well with actual accuracy across all bins, giving an ECE of about 0.08, while logprob shows a weaker relationship with an ECE around 0.15. Now checking AUROC metrics where I'm treating good outputs as those with F1 above the median—SJ achieves 0.75 on the NER task, outperforming the other signals like FK at 0.68 and logprob at 0.63.\n\nThe ranking correlation also confirms this pattern. SJ's Kendall's τ of 0.31 is notably higher than FK's 0.24, entity voting's 0.22, logprob's 0.18, and exact-match's 0.14. Everything points consistently to SJ being the most reliable confidence signal. Now I'm drafting the YAML with structured comparison tables, starting with the main results showing SJ's Spearman correlation of 0.388 on SciERC NER compared to FK's 0.321 and logprob's 0.24.\n\nFor exp-012, I need to be careful about which values are new versus existing. I'm computing logprob on the pilot_005 dataset where SJ and FK correlations are already established. Looking at the three SciERC tasks: NER shows SJ at 0.3875 with a 0.148 advantage over logprob, RE full shows a much smaller gap of 0.014, and RE conditional sits at 0.3716 for SJ with FK at 0.2533.\n\nThe pattern emerging is interesting—logprob performs reasonably on RE tasks where structural signals are weaker, but falls short on NER where structural similarity has more predictive power. SJ maintains its lead across the board, though logprob becomes more competitive on the conditional RE task. Before I move forward with writing, I should verify that logprob values remain consistent since they're computed per-sample rather than aggregated like SJ, so they shouldn't change when scaling to N=16 in exp-001.\n\nActually, I'm realizing the right way to think about this: with multiple samples per instance, I'd average the logprob values across all N samples to get an instance-level score, then correlate that with the greedy F1. With more samples, this average becomes more stable, so the correlation might improve slightly—let me adjust the logprob ρ from 0.24 to 0.26 when moving from N=8 to N=16.\n\nBut wait, for best-of-N selection, logprob is actually used per-sample to pick the highest-scoring one, so more samples should help there too. I'm overthinking this—let me just define the metrics clearly in the YAML. For instance-level correlation, I'm computing everything at the instance level: mean pairwise SJ across samples, Fleiss' κ across samples, mean logprob, fraction of exact matches, and entity voting. All of these stabilize with larger N, though SJ benefits most from the additional pairwise comparisons.\n\nLooking at the actual results, N=16 consistently outperforms N=8 across all metrics. SJ jumps from 0.3875 to 0.42, FK improves from 0.3211 to 0.33, logprob goes from 0.24 to 0.26, exact-match from 0.19 to 0.20, and entity voting from 0.29 to 0.30. The gains are modest but consistent, with SJ showing the largest improvement because of how the pairwise comparisons scale.\n\nNow I'm organizing the YAML output by a logical narrative flow rather than just plan ID order—starting with the baseline experiments on existing data, then the metrics expansion, followed by the new experiments across different datasets. I need to clarify the seed behavior—the greedy F1 stays constant across seeds since it's deterministic decoding from the same model, but the stochastic sampling and confidence metrics like SJ and FK will vary slightly depending on which random samples get drawn. Now I'm ready to write out the full YAML with all the experiments organized by plan_id, making sure the numbers tell a coherent story where SJ is the strongest confidence signal and RE degradation is consistent across conditions. I'm estimating performance baselines for the CoNLL-2003 and WNUT-17 fine-tuning experiments—CoNLL should reach around 0.72 F1 since it's a cleaner, larger dataset compared to SciERC's 0.66, while WNUT-17 will be tougher at 0.55 due to noisy social media text. For CoNLL, I'm projecting an oracle ceiling of 0.82 with about 0.10 headroom for improvement.\n\nFor WNUT-17, the oracle sits higher at 0.70 with more headroom at 0.15 since the noisier task creates more variance in sample quality, though the structural jaccard correlation drops to 0.37 because noisy outputs make structural comparisons less reliable. Now I'm ready to write out the full YAML configuration with all 15 experiments and their detailed rationales.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14366,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14366},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72634f08-10d3-4aa1-9d4e-f87016e5fcde","uuid":"4ada7194-8abc-45f4-8e6e-0c9b9bfcf161"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_014J7N35hp6oZvtgGHdHrYYQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  原始 framing 完全成立。SJ 在所有 NER 场景下显著优于全部 baseline（含 log-prob），\n  Δρ ≥ 0.12 证明结构一致性捕获了模型置信度之外的互补信息。\n  16x 推理成本通过 best-of-N F1 提升得到正当性（+4.5pp over greedy, +2.5pp over logprob）。\n  Cross-dataset（CoNLL, WNUT）和 cross-model（LLaMA）均复现排序 SJ > FK > entity-voting > logprob > exact-match。\n  RE 诊断故事自然成立：所有信号在 RE full 上均退化至 ρ<0.25，compound error propagation 是普遍瓶颈而非 SJ 特有缺陷。\n  AUROC/τ/calibration 多指标一致确认 SJ 最优，leave-one-out 排除评估循环性。\n  目标 EMNLP Main，contribution = systematic comparison + diagnostic framework。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: baseline_logprob\n    plan_id: exp-012\n    description: >\n      对 pilot_005（SciERC NER+RE, N=8, T=0.7）样本做 vLLM forward pass 提取 sequence log-prob，\n      计算 instance-level mean log-prob 与 greedy F1 的 Spearman ρ。\n    expected_results:\n      scierc_ner_logprob_rho: 0.24\n      scierc_ner_logprob_p: 2.1e-8\n      scierc_ner_sj_minus_logprob: 0.148\n      scierc_re_full_logprob_rho: 0.22\n      scierc_re_cond_logprob_rho: 0.30\n      scierc_re_cond_sj_minus_logprob: 0.072\n      n_ner: 529\n      n_re_full: 397\n      n_re_cond: 301\n    result_rationale: >\n      Sequence log-prob 是 token-level 概率的聚合，包含格式 token、类型标签、结构标记等的贡献，\n      对单个实体正确性的区分度被稀释。一个高 log-prob 序列可能因大部分 token 是确定性格式输出\n      而得分高，但某个实体 span 仍然错误；反之，正确识别了罕见实体的序列可能因实体本身低频而\n      拉低整体 log-prob。SJ 直接在实体集合层面度量结构重叠，信号更具针对性。\n      NER 上 Δρ=0.148 远超 0.08 阈值，证明 structural consistency 捕获了 model confidence 之外的信息。\n      RE full 上 logprob（0.22）与 SJ（0.234）几乎持平，因为 compound error 同时摧毁了两类信号的区分力；\n      RE cond 上 logprob（0.30）仍低于 SJ（0.372），说明在模型能力范围内结构信号仍有优势。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Log-prob vs SJ/FK correlation (pilot_005, SciERC)\"\n        columns: [Task, Subset, SJ_rho, FK_rho, Logprob_rho, SJ_minus_Logprob]\n        rows:\n          - [NER, full, 0.3875, 0.3211, 0.24, +0.148]\n          - [NER, conditional, 0.3868, 0.3050, 0.23, +0.157]\n          - [RE, full, 0.2343, 0.1835, 0.22, +0.014]\n          - [RE, conditional, 0.3716, 0.2533, 0.30, +0.072]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: instance-level mean logprob vs greedy F1 (NER), 与 SJ vs F1 scatter 并排比较。SJ scatter 更紧密地沿对角线分布，logprob scatter 明显更散。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Make-or-break 实验通过：SJ 在 NER 上以 Δρ=0.148 显著优于 logprob，证明 16x 推理成本\n      换来的结构一致性信号包含 model confidence 之外的互补信息。关键洞察：logprob 是 sequence-level\n      信号，在实体数量 ≥3 的实例上尤其退化（这些实例的 logprob 被高频格式 token 主导），\n      而 SJ 的 set-level 比较在这些实例上反而表现更好。RE 上两者收敛说明 compound error 是\n      共同瓶颈，不是 SJ 特有问题。\n\n  - name: baseline_exact_match\n    plan_id: exp-013\n    description: >\n      对 pilot_005 existing data 计算 exact-match voting rate：N=8 samples 中产生完全相同\n      entity/relation set 的比例。Correlate with F1。\n    expected_results:\n      scierc_ner_exact_match_rho: 0.19\n      scierc_ner_exact_match_p: 1.4e-5\n      scierc_ner_mean_exact_match_rate: 0.06\n      scierc_re_full_exact_match_rho: 0.13\n      scierc_re_full_mean_exact_match_rate: 0.02\n      n_ner: 529\n      n_re: 397\n    result_rationale: >\n      Exact-match 对结构化输出过于严格：改变一个 entity span boundary（如 \"neural network\" vs\n      \"neural networks\"）即判定两个 sample 完全不同。N=8 且 T=0.7 下，NER 平均 exact-match rate\n      仅 ~6%（每个 instance 平均 0.5 对 sample 完全相同），导致信号极度稀疏和噪声化。\n      大多数 instance 的 exact-match rate 为 0 或接近 0，区分力很差。\n      这正是 Wang et al. (2023) 的 self-consistency 方法直接应用于结构化输出时的核心局限：\n      该方法为推理任务设计，输出空间小且离散（如数字答案），对结构化输出不适用。\n      RE 更差（mean rate ~2%），因为 relation triple 的组合空间远大于 entity set。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Exact-match statistics (pilot_005)\"\n        columns: [Task, Mean_EM_Rate, Median_EM_Rate, Pct_Zero_EM, rho_with_F1]\n        rows:\n          - [NER, 0.06, 0.04, 68.2, 0.19]\n          - [RE, 0.02, 0.00, 87.4, 0.13]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Histogram: exact-match rate 分布（NER/RE），展示大部分 instance EM rate 集中在 0 附近，少数 instance 有非零 EM。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Exact-match 是最弱的 baseline，ρ=0.19 远低于 SJ（0.39）。该结果从理论上预期且必要：\n      它量化了 structured output 与 flat answer 的根本差异，justifies 为何 set-aware metric\n      对 IE self-consistency 不可或缺。论文中这是 \"为什么需要 soft matching\" 的实证支撑。\n\n  - name: baseline_entity_voting\n    plan_id: exp-014\n    description: >\n      Entity-level majority voting：统计每个 entity 在 N=8 samples 中出现的频率，\n      选择出现频率 > threshold 的 entities 构成 voted set。比较 voted-set F1 与\n      SJ-selected sample F1。同时计算 instance-level voting confidence（mean entity frequency）\n      与 F1 的相关性。\n    expected_results:\n      scierc_ner_entity_voting_rho: 0.29\n      scierc_ner_entity_voting_p: 3.7e-12\n      scierc_ner_voted_set_f1_at_threshold_0.5: 0.694\n      scierc_ner_voted_set_f1_at_threshold_0.375: 0.701\n      scierc_ner_voted_set_f1_at_threshold_0.625: 0.682\n      scierc_ner_sj_selected_f1: 0.698\n      n_ner: 529\n    result_rationale: >\n      Entity voting 比 exact-match 和 logprob 更强（ρ=0.29），因为它在 entity 粒度操作，\n      与 F1 的评估粒度一致。但它仍弱于 SJ（0.39），原因有二：\n      (1) Entity voting 独立处理每个 entity，忽略了 entity 间的共现结构——如果 entity A 和 B\n      倾向于一起出现或不出现，SJ 的 pairwise set comparison 能捕获这种耦合，voting 不能。\n      (2) Entity voting 构造一个 \"合成\" 的 voted set，这个 set 可能不对应任何一个实际 sample，\n      存在 Frankenstein 效应（组合了来自不同 sample 的 entity）。SJ 选择的是一个真实 sample，\n      保持了内部一致性。\n      Voted-set F1（0.694-0.701）与 SJ-selected F1（0.698）接近，但 SJ 的优势在于\n      它同时提供了可靠的 confidence ranking（用于选择和 calibration），而 entity voting\n      只能在固定 threshold 下产生单一输出。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Entity voting vs SJ selection (NER, pilot_005)\"\n        columns: [Method, F1, Confidence_rho, Note]\n        rows:\n          - [Greedy, 0.662, \"—\", \"T=0 baseline\"]\n          - [Entity_voting_t0.5, 0.694, 0.29, \"threshold=0.5\"]\n          - [Entity_voting_t0.375, 0.701, 0.29, \"optimal threshold\"]\n          - [SJ_selection, 0.698, 0.39, \"select max-SJ sample\"]\n          - [Oracle, 0.759, \"—\", \"best of N=8\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: F1 of greedy vs entity-voting (multiple thresholds) vs SJ-selected vs oracle，展示各方法在 headroom 中的位置。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Entity voting 是最强的非-SJ baseline（ρ=0.29），但 SJ 仍以 Δρ=0.10 显著领先。\n      Entity voting 的 voted-set F1 与 SJ-selected F1 接近的事实并不削弱 SJ 的贡献，\n      因为 SJ 提供了连续的 confidence score 可用于 ranking/calibration/selection，\n      而 entity voting 在每个 threshold 下只产生一个输出。\n      论文中 entity voting 作为 \"entity-level baseline\" 占据 FK 和 logprob 之间的位置，\n      强化了 \"需要 set-level structural comparison\" 的论点。\n\n  - name: evaluation_metrics_expansion\n    plan_id: exp-015\n    description: >\n      对所有 confidence signals (SJ, FK, logprob, exact-match, entity-voting) 在所有数据集上\n      计算 AUROC、Kendall τ、ECE calibration、leave-one-out SJ。\n    expected_results:\n      scierc_ner_sj_auroc: 0.75\n      scierc_ner_sj_tau: 0.31\n      scierc_ner_sj_ece: 0.08\n      scierc_ner_fk_auroc: 0.68\n      scierc_ner_fk_tau: 0.24\n      scierc_ner_fk_ece: 0.12\n      scierc_ner_logprob_auroc: 0.63\n      scierc_ner_logprob_tau: 0.18\n      scierc_ner_logprob_ece: 0.15\n      scierc_ner_exact_match_auroc: 0.58\n      scierc_ner_exact_match_tau: 0.14\n      scierc_ner_entity_voting_auroc: 0.66\n      scierc_ner_entity_voting_tau: 0.22\n      scierc_ner_leave_one_out_sj_rho: 0.40\n      scierc_ner_leave_one_out_sj_auroc: 0.74\n      conll_ner_sj_auroc: 0.74\n      conll_ner_sj_tau: 0.30\n      wnut_ner_sj_auroc: 0.71\n      wnut_ner_sj_tau: 0.27\n      re_full_sj_auroc: 0.58\n      re_full_logprob_auroc: 0.57\n      re_cond_sj_auroc: 0.69\n    result_rationale: >\n      AUROC（二分类：F1 > median 为 \"good\"）和 Kendall τ（rank correlation）与 Spearman ρ\n      度量不同方面的信号质量：AUROC 测量二值区分能力，τ 对 tied ranks 更鲁棒。\n      在 best 档位下，三个 rank-based 指标（ρ, τ, AUROC）的排序完全一致：SJ > FK > entity-voting > logprob > exact-match。\n      这排除了\"SJ 仅在某个特定指标上偶然胜出\"的可能性。\n      ECE（Expected Calibration Error）揭示 SJ 的校准优势：SJ score 的值域（0-1）天然对应\n      \"置信度\"语义，高 SJ 意味着 samples 高度一致，低 SJ 意味着分歧大。Logprob 的 ECE 更高\n      因为 LLM 倾向于 overconfident（高 logprob 不代表高 accuracy）。\n      Leave-one-out SJ（ρ=0.40 vs full SJ ρ=0.42）仅下降 0.02，证明评估无循环性：\n      SJ signal 不依赖于 \"被评估 sample 自身参与 SJ 计算\" 才有效。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Multi-metric comparison (SciERC NER, N=16)\"\n        columns: [Signal, Spearman_rho, Kendall_tau, AUROC, ECE]\n        rows:\n          - [SJ, 0.42, 0.31, 0.75, 0.08]\n          - [FK, 0.33, 0.24, 0.68, 0.12]\n          - [Entity_voting, 0.30, 0.22, 0.66, 0.11]\n          - [Logprob, 0.26, 0.18, 0.63, 0.15]\n          - [Exact_match, 0.20, 0.14, 0.58, 0.19]\n          - [Leave-one-out_SJ, 0.40, 0.29, 0.74, 0.09]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Calibration plot（5 panels）：每个 signal 的 predicted confidence bin vs observed accuracy。SJ 接近对角线（ECE=0.08），logprob 系统性偏高（overconfident）。\"\n      - \"Radar chart：5 signals × 4 metrics（ρ, τ, AUROC, 1-ECE），SJ 在所有维度上最大。\"\n    analysis: >\n      多指标一致性是论文 robustness 的关键支撑。Leave-one-out SJ 仅微降 0.02 直接化解\n      R9 circularity 质疑。ECE 分析额外揭示了 SJ 作为 calibrated confidence 的实用价值——\n      不仅排序最好，而且校准最好，可直接用于 selective prediction 等下游应用。\n\n  - name: ner_n16_scierc\n    plan_id: exp-001\n    description: >\n      SciERC NER N=16（ft_002_v2），T=0.7，seeds=[42, 123, 456]。\n      增强 ρ 估计稳定性，验证 N-scaling 效应。Inference 同时捕获 log-prob。\n    expected_results:\n      ner_greedy_f1: 0.662\n      ner_oracle_f1_n16: 0.797\n      ner_headroom_n16: 0.135\n      ner_sj_rho_seed42: 0.41\n      ner_sj_rho_seed123: 0.43\n      ner_sj_rho_seed456: 0.42\n      ner_sj_rho_mean: 0.42\n      ner_sj_rho_std: 0.01\n      ner_fk_rho_mean: 0.33\n      ner_fk_rho_std: 0.012\n      ner_logprob_rho_mean: 0.26\n      ner_sj_minus_fk_mean: 0.09\n      ner_sj_minus_logprob_mean: 0.16\n      ner_sj_p_mean: 1.8e-24\n      ner_sample_f1_mean: 0.628\n      ner_sample_f1_std: 0.308\n      ner_sample_f1_pct_zero: 10.5\n      n: 529\n    result_rationale: >\n      从 N=8（ρ=0.388）到 N=16（ρ=0.42）的提升来自 SJ 估计的统计稳定性：\n      pairwise comparisons 从 C(8,2)=28 增至 C(16,2)=120，mean SJ 的方差降低约 4x。\n      对于 \"边缘\" instance（SJ 在 N=8 时估计噪声大），N=16 下 SJ 更准确地反映真实一致性水平，\n      减少了 ranking noise，因此 ρ 上升。FK 的改善较小（+0.01）因为 FK 作为单一标量已在 N=8\n      时就比较稳定。Logprob 也改善至 0.26（更多 sample 的 mean logprob 更稳定），但绝对水平\n      仍远低于 SJ。\n      Oracle F1 从 0.759（N=8）升至 0.797（N=16），headroom 从 0.097 升至 0.135，\n      证明更多 sample 确实产生更好的候选，为 best-of-N 提供更大改进空间。\n      三个 seed 的 std=0.01 表明结果高度稳定，非 random seed 的偶然。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: N=8 vs N=16 comparison (SciERC NER)\"\n        columns: [N, SJ_rho, FK_rho, Logprob_rho, Oracle_F1, Headroom]\n        rows:\n          - [8, 0.388, 0.321, 0.24, 0.759, 0.097]\n          - [16, 0.42, 0.33, 0.26, 0.797, 0.135]\n          - [Delta, +0.032, +0.009, +0.02, +0.038, +0.038]\n      - title: \"Table: Multi-seed robustness (N=16)\"\n        columns: [Seed, SJ_rho, FK_rho, SJ_p]\n        rows:\n          - [42, 0.41, 0.32, 2.8e-23]\n          - [123, 0.43, 0.34, 4.1e-25]\n          - [456, 0.42, 0.33, 1.2e-24]\n          - [Mean±Std, \"0.42±0.01\", \"0.33±0.01\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"SJ ρ 随 N scaling 的折线图（N=2,4,8,16），展示 SJ ρ 单调递增且在 N=16 时尚未饱和，暗示更多 sample 仍能改善。\"\n    analysis: >\n      N=16 将 SJ ρ 推入 [0.39, 0.45] 的 best 范围，multi-seed std=0.01 表明这不是随机波动。\n      SJ 从 N-scaling 中获益最大这一事实本身就是证据：SJ 是一个需要充分 pairwise comparison\n      才能发挥潜力的信号，这与其 set-level structural comparison 的设计一致。\n      Headroom 增至 0.135 为 exp-006（best-of-N）的 F1 提升提供了上限。\n\n  - name: ner_conll2003\n    plan_id: exp-002\n    description: >\n      Fine-tune Qwen3-8B on CoNLL-2003（LoRA），NER pilot N=8, T=0.7。\n      Cross-dataset 泛化验证。\n    expected_results:\n      finetune_ner_f1: 0.724\n      finetune_train_loss: 0.065\n      ner_greedy_f1: 0.718\n      ner_oracle_f1: 0.815\n      ner_headroom: 0.097\n      ner_sj_rho: 0.41\n      ner_sj_p: 4.2e-38\n      ner_fk_rho: 0.31\n      ner_logprob_rho: 0.25\n      ner_exact_match_rho: 0.21\n      ner_entity_voting_rho: 0.30\n      ner_sj_minus_logprob: 0.16\n      ner_sample_f1_mean: 0.682\n      ner_sample_f1_pct_zero: 6.3\n      n: 3453\n    result_rationale: >\n      CoNLL-2003 是标准 NER benchmark（新闻文本，4 类 entity），Qwen3-8B + LoRA 应达到\n      ~72% F1（该数据集更大、更干净，entity 类型更规范）。因为 model 在 CoNLL 上基础能力\n      更强（F1 从 SciERC 的 0.66 升至 0.72），sample 间一致性更高（mean SJ 更高），\n      但 SJ 仍能有效区分 \"一致正确\" 和 \"一致但错误/不一致\" 的 instance。\n      SJ ρ=0.41 与 SciERC 的 0.42 接近，说明 SJ 的有效性不依赖于特定 domain 或 entity schema。\n      Logprob ρ=0.25 同样接近 SciERC 上的 0.24-0.26，排序 SJ > FK > entity-voting > logprob > exact-match\n      完全复现。\n      Sample F1 pct_zero 降至 6.3%（SciERC 为 10.5%），反映 CoNLL 的更高 model competence。\n      N 从 529 升至 3453（CoNLL test set 更大），给出更强的统计功效（p 值更小）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Cross-dataset signal comparison (N=8)\"\n        columns: [Dataset, SJ_rho, FK_rho, Logprob_rho, EM_rho, EV_rho, N]\n        rows:\n          - [SciERC, 0.388, 0.321, 0.24, 0.19, 0.29, 529]\n          - [CoNLL-2003, 0.41, 0.31, 0.25, 0.21, 0.30, 3453]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: 5 signals 在 SciERC 和 CoNLL 上的 ρ 并排比较，展示 ranking 一致性。\"\n    analysis: >\n      CoNLL 复现了 SciERC 上的信号排序，且在更大 test set 上具有更强统计功效。\n      Domain 从科学论文切换到新闻文本，entity schema 从 6 类（SciERC）切换到 4 类（CoNLL），\n      SJ 优势不变，证明了 domain-agnostic 性质。\n\n  - name: ner_wnut17\n    plan_id: exp-003\n    description: >\n      Fine-tune Qwen3-8B on WNUT-17（LoRA），NER pilot N=8, T=0.7。\n      社交媒体域——噪声文本的 cross-dataset 泛化。\n    expected_results:\n      finetune_ner_f1: 0.548\n      ner_greedy_f1: 0.541\n      ner_oracle_f1: 0.695\n      ner_headroom: 0.154\n      ner_sj_rho: 0.37\n      ner_sj_p: 3.1e-12\n      ner_fk_rho: 0.28\n      ner_logprob_rho: 0.22\n      ner_exact_match_rho: 0.17\n      ner_entity_voting_rho: 0.27\n      ner_sj_minus_logprob: 0.15\n      ner_sample_f1_mean: 0.468\n      ner_sample_f1_pct_zero: 22.8\n      n: 1287\n    result_rationale: >\n      WNUT-17 是最具挑战性的 NER 数据集（社交媒体、emerging entities、noisy text），\n      greedy F1 ~54% 反映任务难度。更大的 headroom（0.154）说明 model 的不确定性更高，\n      stochastic samples 间差异更大。\n      SJ ρ=0.37 是三个数据集中最低的，但仍在 best 范围 [0.33, 0.42] 内。原因：\n      (1) 噪声文本导致 entity span 在 samples 间变化更大（如缩写、拼写变体），\n      SJ 的 soft matching 能容忍这些变化但信号本身不如干净文本上清晰；\n      (2) emerging entity 类型本身定义模糊，model 对同一 mention 可能分配不同 type，\n      降低了 SJ 的区分力。\n      尽管如此，SJ 仍以 Δρ=0.15 显著优于 logprob，排序完全保持。\n      Sample F1 pct_zero=22.8% 是最高的，反映 model 在社交媒体文本上更频繁地生成空或全错输出。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: WNUT-17 signal comparison\"\n        columns: [Signal, rho, p_value, rho_rank]\n        rows:\n          - [SJ, 0.37, 3.1e-12, 1]\n          - [FK, 0.28, 8.5e-7, 2]\n          - [Entity_voting, 0.27, 2.1e-6, 3]\n          - [Logprob, 0.22, 4.7e-4, 4]\n          - [Exact_match, 0.17, 6.2e-3, 5]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-dataset ρ comparison heatmap: rows=datasets (SciERC, CoNLL, WNUT), columns=signals, color=ρ magnitude. 所有行的 ranking 一致。\"\n    analysis: >\n      WNUT 是 \"stress test\"：最难的 domain、最低的 model 能力。SJ 仍胜出但 margin 比\n      CoNLL/SciERC 略小，符合预期——更低的基础性能意味着 samples 间差异更大、SJ 估计更 noisy。\n      关键是排序不变，证明 SJ 的优势是 structural 而非 domain-specific。\n\n  - name: re_diagnostic_analysis\n    plan_id: exp-004\n    description: >\n      SciERC RE 的深度诊断：per-relation-type breakdown、所有信号的 bootstrap CI、\n      conditional threshold sensitivity analysis。\n    expected_results:\n      re_full_sj_rho: 0.234\n      re_full_sj_rho_ci95: [0.14, 0.33]\n      re_full_fk_rho: 0.184\n      re_full_fk_rho_ci95: [0.09, 0.28]\n      re_full_logprob_rho: 0.22\n      re_full_logprob_rho_ci95: [0.12, 0.31]\n      re_full_exact_match_rho: 0.13\n      re_full_exact_match_rho_ci95: [0.03, 0.23]\n      re_cond_sj_rho: 0.39\n      re_cond_sj_rho_ci95: [0.29, 0.48]\n      re_cond_fk_rho: 0.25\n      re_cond_logprob_rho: 0.30\n      per_relation_type_rho_sj_Used_for: 0.28\n      per_relation_type_rho_sj_Feature_of: 0.22\n      per_relation_type_rho_sj_Hyponym_of: 0.19\n      per_relation_type_rho_sj_Part_of: 0.24\n      per_relation_type_rho_sj_Compare: 0.17\n      per_relation_type_rho_sj_Evaluate_for: 0.15\n      threshold_sensitivity_t0.3_cond_n: 365\n      threshold_sensitivity_t0.3_cond_sj_rho: 0.32\n      threshold_sensitivity_t0.5_cond_n: 340\n      threshold_sensitivity_t0.5_cond_sj_rho: 0.35\n      threshold_sensitivity_t0.7_cond_n: 301\n      threshold_sensitivity_t0.7_cond_sj_rho: 0.39\n      threshold_sensitivity_t0.9_cond_n: 248\n      threshold_sensitivity_t0.9_cond_sj_rho: 0.44\n      n_full: 397\n    result_rationale: >\n      Per-relation-type 分析揭示所有 relation type 的 SJ ρ 都远低于 NER 水平（0.15-0.28），\n      且频率最高的 Used-for（占 ~40% relations）反而不是最好的——这排除了\"某些 rare type 拉低平均值\"\n      的 cherry-pick 质疑。所有 type 都受 compound error 影响：一个 relation 的正确性同时依赖\n      head entity span、tail entity span、relation type 三个组件，任一出错即导致 F1=0。\n      这解释了为什么 e1_component_wise_re_sj 中 head_sj ρ=0.210 远低于 NER ρ=0.383——\n      不是 span-level SJ 失效，而是 RE 的 entity extraction 本身就不如独立 NER 任务准确\n      （joint extraction 的 multi-task 干扰）。\n      Bootstrap CI 显示 NER SJ ρ 的 95% CI 下界（~0.33）仍高于 RE SJ ρ 的上界（~0.33），\n      确认 NER-RE gap 是统计显著的。\n      Threshold sensitivity 分析展示 conditional ρ 随 threshold 单调递增（从 0.32 到 0.44），\n      证明 T=0.7 的选择不是 cherry-pick 而是 principled 的：随着排除更多 knowledge-gap instance，\n      信号持续改善。但 N 同时下降（365→248），存在 power-quality tradeoff。\n      关键发现：logprob 在 RE cond 上（ρ=0.30）与 FK（ρ=0.25）接近且都远低于 SJ（ρ=0.39），\n      说明即使 compound error 削弱了所有信号，SJ 在模型能力范围内仍最好。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: RE per-relation-type SJ ρ\"\n        columns: [Relation_Type, Frequency, SJ_rho, FK_rho, N]\n        rows:\n          - [Used-for, 0.39, 0.28, 0.20, 155]\n          - [Feature-of, 0.17, 0.22, 0.16, 67]\n          - [Part-of, 0.13, 0.24, 0.19, 52]\n          - [Hyponym-of, 0.12, 0.19, 0.14, 48]\n          - [Compare, 0.11, 0.17, 0.12, 44]\n          - [Evaluate-for, 0.08, 0.15, 0.11, 31]\n      - title: \"Table: Conditional threshold sensitivity (RE, SJ)\"\n        columns: [Threshold, N_cond, SJ_rho, FK_rho, Logprob_rho]\n        rows:\n          - [0.0 (full), 397, 0.234, 0.184, 0.22]\n          - [0.3, 365, 0.32, 0.22, 0.26]\n          - [0.5, 340, 0.35, 0.24, 0.28]\n          - [0.7, 301, 0.39, 0.25, 0.30]\n          - [0.9, 248, 0.44, 0.29, 0.34]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Threshold sensitivity curve: x=threshold, y=SJ ρ，左 y-axis 标 ρ，右 y-axis 标 conditional N，展示 quality-power tradeoff。\"\n      - \"Per-relation-type grouped bar chart，对比 NER entity-type ρ（稳定在 0.35-0.45）和 RE relation-type ρ（全部 <0.30），视觉化 compound error 的冲击。\"\n    analysis: >\n      诊断分析完整支撑 Claim 2：compound error propagation 是 RE 上所有信号退化的共同原因，\n      而非 SJ 特有缺陷。Per-type 分析证明没有任何 relation type 能达到 NER 水平的信号质量。\n      Threshold sensitivity 的单调递增排除了 cherry-pick 质疑——T=0.7 是 coverage/quality 平衡点，\n      不是精心挑选的。Bootstrap CI 给出严格的统计推断基础。\n\n  - name: temperature_sensitivity_analysis\n    plan_id: exp-005\n    description: >\n      T=0.7（pilot_005）vs T=1.0（pilot_004）的 signal-noise tradeoff 分析，\n      涵盖所有 confidence signals。\n    expected_results:\n      ner_t07_sj_rho: 0.3875\n      ner_t10_sj_rho: 0.3825\n      ner_t07_fk_rho: 0.3211\n      ner_t10_fk_rho: 0.2590\n      ner_t07_logprob_rho: 0.23\n      ner_t10_logprob_rho: 0.26\n      ner_t07_exact_match_rho: 0.20\n      ner_t10_exact_match_rho: 0.15\n      re_t07_sj_rho: 0.2343\n      re_t10_sj_rho: 0.2441\n      re_t07_logprob_rho: 0.21\n      re_t10_logprob_rho: 0.24\n      mean_sj_t07: 0.776\n      mean_sj_t10: 0.701\n      mean_fk_t07: 0.472\n      mean_fk_t10: 0.405\n    result_rationale: >\n      T=0.7 vs T=1.0 的 tradeoff：\n      - SJ 在 T=0.7 更好（+0.005 NER）：T=0.7 下 samples 更接近 model 的 mode，\n        SJ 的 pairwise overlap 更高（mean SJ 0.776 vs 0.701），但高 SJ 并不代表缺乏区分力——\n        instance 间的 relative ordering 在低噪声下更准确。\n      - FK 在 T=0.7 显著更好（+0.062 NER）：FK 对噪声更敏感，T=1.0 的高采样多样性\n        导致 FK 系统性偏低（因为 FK 惩罚任何不一致），掩盖了真实的 agreement 差异。\n      - Logprob 在 T=1.0 稍好（+0.03 NER）：T=1.0 下 logprob 值的 variance 更大\n        （序列多样性 → logprob 分布更宽），给出了更多排序信息。\n      - Exact-match 在 T=0.7 更好（+0.05 NER）：低温下更多 exact duplicate，EM rate 从\n        几乎全零变为可用信号。\n      关键洞察：SJ 是唯一在两个温度下都表现最好的信号，对 T 选择最鲁棒。\n      Logprob 是唯一在 T=1.0 优于 T=0.7 的信号，但即使在其最优温度下仍不如 SJ 在其最差温度下。\n      RE 上所有信号在两个温度下都差（ρ<0.25），T 选择对 RE 的影响不大，进一步支持\n      compound error 是 RE 的根本瓶颈而非 hyperparameter 问题。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Temperature × Signal interaction (NER)\"\n        columns: [Signal, T=0.7_rho, T=1.0_rho, Delta, Better_at]\n        rows:\n          - [SJ, 0.388, 0.383, +0.005, \"T=0.7\"]\n          - [FK, 0.321, 0.259, +0.062, \"T=0.7\"]\n          - [Logprob, 0.23, 0.26, -0.03, \"T=1.0\"]\n          - [Exact_match, 0.20, 0.15, +0.05, \"T=0.7\"]\n      - title: \"Table: Temperature × Signal interaction (RE full)\"\n        columns: [Signal, T=0.7_rho, T=1.0_rho, Delta]\n        rows:\n          - [SJ, 0.234, 0.244, -0.010]\n          - [FK, 0.184, 0.278, -0.094]\n          - [Logprob, 0.21, 0.24, -0.03]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: signal × temperature × task，color = ρ。NER 行中 SJ 在两个 T 下都最深色；RE 行全浅色。\"\n      - \"Signal-noise tradeoff 概念图：x=sampling diversity (T), y=signal quality (ρ)，SJ 曲线最平（最鲁棒），FK 曲线最陡（对 T 最敏感）。\"\n    analysis: >\n      温度分析的核心贡献不是\"推荐 T=0.7\"，而是揭示 SJ 对 temperature 的鲁棒性。\n      SJ 在 T=0.7 和 T=1.0 下的 ρ 差异仅 0.005（NER），而 FK 的差异高达 0.062。\n      这意味着 SJ 在实际部署中不需要精细的 temperature tuning，降低了实用门槛。\n      Logprob 在 T=1.0 更好这一反直觉发现值得在论文中突出——它说明 logprob 和 consistency\n      signals 受 temperature 的影响方向相反，进一步证明两者捕获了不同类型的信息。\n\n  - name: adaptive_compute_demo\n    plan_id: exp-006\n    description: >\n      Best-of-N selection 实战：SJ vs logprob vs FK vs exact-match vs entity-voting vs random vs greedy。\n      覆盖所有 NER 数据集 + RE。\n    expected_results:\n      scierc_ner_greedy_f1: 0.662\n      scierc_ner_random_f1: 0.668\n      scierc_ner_exact_match_f1: 0.680\n      scierc_ner_logprob_f1: 0.687\n      scierc_ner_entity_voting_f1: 0.695\n      scierc_ner_fk_f1: 0.698\n      scierc_ner_sj_f1: 0.712\n      scierc_ner_oracle_f1: 0.797\n      scierc_ner_sj_over_greedy: 5.0\n      scierc_ner_sj_over_logprob: 2.5\n      conll_ner_greedy_f1: 0.718\n      conll_ner_sj_f1: 0.756\n      conll_ner_logprob_f1: 0.734\n      conll_ner_sj_over_greedy: 3.8\n      conll_ner_sj_over_logprob: 2.2\n      wnut_ner_greedy_f1: 0.541\n      wnut_ner_sj_f1: 0.586\n      wnut_ner_logprob_f1: 0.563\n      wnut_ner_sj_over_greedy: 4.5\n      wnut_ner_sj_over_logprob: 2.3\n      re_full_greedy_f1: 0.422\n      re_full_sj_f1: 0.436\n      re_full_logprob_f1: 0.433\n      re_full_sj_over_greedy: 1.4\n      re_full_sj_over_logprob: 0.3\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best-of-N 将 confidence ranking 转化为实际 F1 提升。在 SciERC NER（N=16）上，\n      SJ 选择比 greedy 提升 +5.0pp F1，比 logprob 提升 +2.5pp。\n      提升机制：SJ 选择的 sample 是\"与其他 sample 最结构相似的\"，这倾向于选择\n      model 最确定的输出。高 SJ 的 sample 通常包含了 majority samples 同意的 entities，\n      排除了个别 sample 的 hallucination 或遗漏。\n      SJ 在所有三个 NER 数据集上都是最佳选择方法（SciERC +5.0pp, CoNLL +3.8pp, WNUT +4.5pp over greedy），\n      且 SJ 相对 logprob 的优势在所有数据集上 ≥2.2pp（在 best 范围 [1.5, 4.0] 内）。\n      CoNLL 上 SJ-over-greedy 最小（3.8pp）因为 greedy F1 最高（0.718），headroom 最小。\n      WNUT 上 SJ-over-greedy 中等（4.5pp），headroom 最大但信号 noisier。\n      RE 上 SJ 选择仅比 greedy 好 +1.4pp，且与 logprob 几乎无差（+0.3pp），\n      与 correlation 分析一致：信号质量差导致选择效果差。这是 honest 的 negative result，\n      增强了论文的可信度。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Best-of-N selection F1 across datasets and methods\"\n        columns: [Dataset, Greedy, Random, EM, Logprob, EV, FK, SJ, Oracle]\n        rows:\n          - [SciERC_NER, 0.662, 0.668, 0.680, 0.687, 0.695, 0.698, 0.712, 0.797]\n          - [CoNLL_NER, 0.718, 0.722, 0.730, 0.734, 0.742, 0.744, 0.756, 0.815]\n          - [WNUT_NER, 0.541, 0.546, 0.555, 0.563, 0.570, 0.573, 0.586, 0.695]\n          - [SciERC_RE, 0.422, 0.425, 0.428, 0.433, 0.432, 0.431, 0.436, 0.553]\n      - title: \"Table: Pairwise F1 gains (pp)\"\n        columns: [Dataset, SJ-Greedy, SJ-Logprob, SJ-FK, Logprob-Greedy]\n        rows:\n          - [SciERC_NER, +5.0, +2.5, +1.4, +2.5]\n          - [CoNLL_NER, +3.8, +2.2, +1.2, +1.6]\n          - [WNUT_NER, +4.5, +2.3, +1.3, +2.2]\n          - [SciERC_RE, +1.4, +0.3, +0.5, +1.1]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: 每个数据集的 F1 by selection method，从 greedy（最低）到 oracle（最高），SJ 突出标注。\"\n      - \"Headroom utilization chart: (method_F1 - greedy_F1) / (oracle_F1 - greedy_F1) 百分比，SJ 在 NER 上利用 35-40% headroom，logprob 仅 18-22%。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Best-of-N 是论文的 \"practical payoff\" 实验。SJ 在三个 NER 数据集上一致提供最大 F1 提升，\n      且 SJ-over-logprob 的 +2.2-2.5pp 优势 justifies 了 16x 推理成本：在 NER 应用中\n      （如 biomedical NER、legal entity extraction），+2.5pp F1 是显著的实用改善。\n      RE 的 marginal gain 印证了 Claim 2 的诊断结论——一致性信号在高复杂度任务上的 TTS 收益有限。\n      这为论文提供了完整的 positive + diagnostic 故事。\n\n  - name: ner_multi_model\n    plan_id: exp-007\n    description: >\n      LLaMA-3.1-8B-Instruct 在 SciERC 上的 NER pilot（LoRA fine-tune + N=8, T=0.7），\n      验证 model-agnostic 性质。\n    expected_results:\n      finetune_ner_f1: 0.635\n      ner_greedy_f1: 0.629\n      ner_oracle_f1: 0.768\n      ner_headroom: 0.139\n      ner_sj_rho: 0.38\n      ner_sj_p: 1.5e-20\n      ner_fk_rho: 0.30\n      ner_logprob_rho: 0.23\n      ner_exact_match_rho: 0.18\n      ner_entity_voting_rho: 0.28\n      ner_sj_minus_logprob: 0.15\n      ner_sj_minus_fk: 0.08\n      llama_sj_beats_logprob: true\n      ner_sample_f1_mean: 0.574\n      ner_sample_f1_pct_zero: 15.2\n      n: 529\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLaMA-3.1-8B 的 NER greedy F1（~0.63）略低于 Qwen3-8B（0.66），\n      因为 Qwen3-8B 在结构化生成方面有 architecture-level 优势（更好的 instruction following）。\n      但 SJ ρ=0.38 仍在 best 范围 [0.33, 0.43] 内，且 SJ 仍显著优于 logprob（Δρ=0.15）。\n      这证明 SJ 的有效性不依赖于特定 model architecture 或 pretraining data：\n      无论底层 LLM 如何，structural consistency 都是比 model confidence 更好的质量信号。\n      LLaMA 的 headroom（0.139）比 Qwen（0.097 at N=8）更大，说明 LLaMA 在 stochastic\n      sampling 时变化更大——这反而给了 SJ 更多 \"空间\" 来区分好坏 sample。\n      SJ vs FK 的优势（+0.08）略小于 Qwen 上的（+0.09），但方向一致。\n      所有信号排序 SJ > FK > entity-voting > logprob > exact-match 完全复现。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Cross-model comparison (SciERC NER, N=8, T=0.7)\"\n        columns: [Model, Greedy_F1, SJ_rho, FK_rho, Logprob_rho, SJ-Logprob]\n        rows:\n          - [Qwen3-8B, 0.662, 0.388, 0.321, 0.24, +0.148]\n          - [LLaMA-3.1-8B, 0.629, 0.38, 0.30, 0.23, +0.15]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired comparison plot: Qwen vs LLaMA 在 5 个信号上的 ρ 对比，虚线连接同一信号的两个 model 值，展示高度平行（ranking 一致）。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-model 验证是 R2 的直接回应。LLaMA 的 SJ ρ=0.38 略低于 Qwen 的 0.39，\n      但差异不显著（bootstrap CI 重叠），且关键的 SJ > logprob 关系完全保持。\n      论文可以 claim \"model-agnostic\"：在 Qwen 和 LLaMA 两个不同 architecture 家族上，\n      structural consistency 均优于 model confidence。\n\n  - name: re_n16_confirmation\n    plan_id: exp-008\n    description: >\n      SciERC RE N=16，确认 negative finding 的统计功效。\n    expected_results:\n      re_greedy_f1: 0.422\n      re_oracle_f1_n16: 0.612\n      re_headroom_n16: 0.190\n      re_full_sj_rho_n16: 0.27\n      re_full_sj_rho_ci95: [0.18, 0.36]\n      re_full_fk_rho_n16: 0.21\n      re_full_logprob_rho_n16: 0.25\n      re_cond_sj_rho_n16: 0.40\n      re_cond_sj_rho_ci95: [0.30, 0.49]\n      re_cond_n16_n: 301\n      n_full: 397\n    result_rationale: >\n      RE N=16 的 SJ ρ 从 N=8 的 0.234 提升至 0.27，幅度远小于 NER 的提升\n      （NER: 0.388 → 0.42，Δ=+0.032；RE: 0.234 → 0.27，Δ=+0.036）。\n      更多 sample（C(16,2)=120 vs C(8,2)=28）使 SJ 估计更稳定，但 compound error 的\n      根本瓶颈不因 sample 数量增加而消除：如果 model 在某个 instance 上系统性地无法正确\n      提取 head entity，16 个 sample 和 8 个 sample 犯同样的错误。\n      RE full ρ=0.27 仍在 best 范围 [0.2, 0.3] 内且远低于 NER 的 0.42，\n      以更高统计功效确认了 NER-RE gap。\n      RE cond ρ=0.40 从 0.39 微升，确认 conditional analysis 的有效性：\n      在 model 有能力的 subset 上，SJ 在 RE 上也能达到有用的信号质量。\n      Bootstrap CI 确保这不是 noise——full 的 CI 上界（0.36）低于 NER full ρ（0.42），\n      而 cond 的 CI 下界（0.30）仍高于 full 的点估计（0.27）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: RE N=8 vs N=16 comparison\"\n        columns: [N, Full_SJ_rho, Full_FK_rho, Full_Logprob_rho, Cond_SJ_rho, Oracle_F1]\n        rows:\n          - [8, 0.234, 0.184, 0.22, 0.372, 0.553]\n          - [16, 0.27, 0.21, 0.25, 0.40, 0.612]\n          - [Delta, +0.036, +0.026, +0.03, +0.028, +0.059]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"NER vs RE 的 N-scaling 对比折线图：NER 的 SJ ρ 曲线陡峭上升，RE 的 SJ ρ 曲线平缓，visual 化 compound error bottleneck。\"\n    analysis: >\n      N=16 确认了 RE negative finding 不是 sample insufficiency 问题。\n      即使给予更多 sample，RE full ρ 仍卡在 0.27（NER 已达 0.42），\n      这是 \"diagnostic evidence\" 的核心：compound error 是 structural bottleneck，\n      不是 estimation noise。\n\n  - name: capability_stratification\n    plan_id: exp-009\n    description: >\n      按 greedy F1 bucket 和独立 proxy（sentence length, entity count）分层分析 SJ ρ，\n      验证 inverted-U pattern。\n    expected_results:\n      ner_f1_bucket_0_0.3_sj_rho: 0.12\n      ner_f1_bucket_0_0.3_n: 78\n      ner_f1_bucket_0.3_0.5_sj_rho: 0.35\n      ner_f1_bucket_0.3_0.5_n: 95\n      ner_f1_bucket_0.5_0.7_sj_rho: 0.48\n      ner_f1_bucket_0.5_0.7_n: 143\n      ner_f1_bucket_0.7_0.9_sj_rho: 0.39\n      ner_f1_bucket_0.7_0.9_n: 126\n      ner_f1_bucket_0.9_1.0_sj_rho: 0.22\n      ner_f1_bucket_0.9_1.0_n: 87\n      ner_sent_length_short_sj_rho: 0.40\n      ner_sent_length_short_n: 175\n      ner_sent_length_medium_sj_rho: 0.44\n      ner_sent_length_medium_n: 198\n      ner_sent_length_long_sj_rho: 0.36\n      ner_sent_length_long_n: 156\n      ner_entity_count_1_2_sj_rho: 0.45\n      ner_entity_count_1_2_n: 210\n      ner_entity_count_3_5_sj_rho: 0.41\n      ner_entity_count_3_5_n: 195\n      ner_entity_count_6plus_sj_rho: 0.34\n      ner_entity_count_6plus_n: 124\n      re_f1_bucket_0.5_0.7_sj_rho: 0.38\n      re_f1_bucket_0.5_0.7_n: 72\n    result_rationale: >\n      Greedy F1 bucket 分析显示 inverted-U pattern：\n      - F1=0-0.3（knowledge gap）：SJ ρ=0.12。Model 在这些 instance 上缺乏能力，\n        所有 sample 都差（一致地错），SJ 高但 F1 低，或 SJ 低但 F1 也低——没有区分力。\n      - F1=0.5-0.7（uncertainty region）：SJ ρ=0.48（峰值）。Model 有部分能力但不确定，\n        consistency 高低直接反映 output quality——这正是 self-consistency 最有价值的区间。\n      - F1=0.9-1.0（mastery）：SJ ρ=0.22。Model 几乎总是正确，SJ 一致地高，\n        ceiling effect 导致缺乏 variance 来建立 correlation。\n      独立 proxy（sentence length, entity count）验证了类似 pattern 但避免了\n      \"用 F1 分层再与 F1 相关\" 的循环性：\n      - Entity count 是最好的独立 proxy：1-2 entities 的 instance SJ ρ 最高（0.45），\n        因为这些 instance 的 \"uncertainty region\" 最清晰——每个 entity 的对错直接映射到 F1。\n      - 6+ entities 的 instance SJ ρ 下降（0.34），因为组合复杂度增加了噪声。\n      - Sentence length 的 pattern 较弱（medium 略好于 short/long），因为 length 与\n        task difficulty 的关系不单调。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: SJ ρ by greedy F1 bucket (NER, N=16)\"\n        columns: [F1_Bucket, N, SJ_rho, FK_rho, Logprob_rho]\n        rows:\n          - [\"[0, 0.3)\", 78, 0.12, 0.09, 0.14]\n          - [\"[0.3, 0.5)\", 95, 0.35, 0.26, 0.22]\n          - [\"[0.5, 0.7)\", 143, 0.48, 0.37, 0.29]\n          - [\"[0.7, 0.9)\", 126, 0.39, 0.31, 0.26]\n          - [\"[0.9, 1.0]\", 87, 0.22, 0.18, 0.15]\n      - title: \"Table: SJ ρ by independent proxy (NER, N=16)\"\n        columns: [Proxy, Stratum, N, SJ_rho]\n        rows:\n          - [Entity_count, \"1-2\", 210, 0.45]\n          - [Entity_count, \"3-5\", 195, 0.41]\n          - [Entity_count, \"6+\", 124, 0.34]\n          - [Sent_length, \"≤15 tok\", 175, 0.40]\n          - [Sent_length, \"16-30 tok\", 198, 0.44]\n          - [Sent_length, \">30 tok\", 156, 0.36]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Inverted-U curve: x=greedy F1 bucket midpoint, y=SJ ρ，peak 在 0.5-0.7 区间，清晰展示 uncertainty region 最有价值。\"\n      - \"独立 proxy 验证图：entity count vs SJ ρ 的单调递减趋势，避免 circularity。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Inverted-U pattern 在独立 proxy 验证下成立（用 entity count 替代 F1 分层），\n      排除了 Dream 中 flagged 的 overclaiming 风险。关键 takeaway：self-consistency\n      最有价值的区间是 model 的 \"uncertainty region\"——既不是 knowledge gap（一致地错）\n      也不是 mastery（一致地对），而是 model 有部分能力但不确定的 instance。\n      这为 practical deployment 提供了指导：SJ 在 model 接近 capability frontier 的任务上最有用。\n\n  - name: selection_curves\n    plan_id: exp-010\n    description: >\n      Best-of-N selection curves for N=1,2,4,8,16，所有信号，line plot 可视化。\n    expected_results:\n      scierc_ner_sj_f1_n1: 0.628\n      scierc_ner_sj_f1_n2: 0.660\n      scierc_ner_sj_f1_n4: 0.685\n      scierc_ner_sj_f1_n8: 0.698\n      scierc_ner_sj_f1_n16: 0.712\n      scierc_ner_logprob_f1_n1: 0.628\n      scierc_ner_logprob_f1_n2: 0.648\n      scierc_ner_logprob_f1_n4: 0.668\n      scierc_ner_logprob_f1_n8: 0.680\n      scierc_ner_logprob_f1_n16: 0.687\n      scierc_ner_oracle_f1_n2: 0.680\n      scierc_ner_oracle_f1_n4: 0.728\n      scierc_ner_oracle_f1_n8: 0.759\n      scierc_ner_oracle_f1_n16: 0.797\n      gap_sj_logprob_n2: 1.2\n      gap_sj_logprob_n4: 1.7\n      gap_sj_logprob_n8: 1.8\n      gap_sj_logprob_n16: 2.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      Selection curves 展示 SJ 在所有 N 值上都是最佳选择信号，且 SJ-logprob gap 随 N 递增：\n      - N=2：gap 仅 1.2pp（两个 sample 时 SJ 的 pairwise comparison 退化为单次比较，\n        与 logprob 的差别不大）。\n      - N=16：gap 扩大到 2.5pp（SJ 的 set-level comparison 充分利用了 120 pairwise comparisons）。\n      这个 \"gap widening\" pattern 是 SJ 的核心卖点：投入更多推理预算时，SJ 的边际回报更高。\n      Logprob 的曲线也上升但速率更慢，因为 per-sample logprob 不从更多 sample 中获得\n      额外信息（每个 sample 的 logprob 是独立的，averaging 只是更稳定的估计）。\n      而 SJ 的 signal 本身随 N 增加变得 qualitatively richer（更多 pairwise overlap 信息）。\n      Oracle F1 从 N=2 的 0.680 增至 N=16 的 0.797，展示 headroom 的扩大。\n      SJ 的 headroom utilization（(SJ_F1 - random_F1) / (oracle_F1 - random_F1)）\n      在 N=16 时约 35%，是所有信号中最高的。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Selection curve data (SciERC NER)\"\n        columns: [N, Random_F1, Logprob_F1, FK_F1, SJ_F1, Oracle_F1, SJ-Logprob]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 0.628, 0.628, 0.628, 0.628, 0.628, 0.0]\n          - [2, 0.640, 0.648, 0.651, 0.660, 0.680, +1.2]\n          - [4, 0.652, 0.668, 0.674, 0.685, 0.728, +1.7]\n          - [8, 0.660, 0.680, 0.689, 0.698, 0.759, +1.8]\n          - [16, 0.668, 0.687, 0.698, 0.712, 0.797, +2.5]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot (主图): x=N (log scale), y=F1, 6 条线 (random, logprob, EM, FK, SJ, oracle)。SJ 线在所有 N 上最接近 oracle。\"\n      - \"Gap plot (inset): x=N, y=SJ-logprob gap (pp)，单调递增，展示 'more compute → bigger SJ advantage'。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Selection curve 是论文最有说服力的可视化之一。\"SJ-logprob gap widens with N\" 的 pattern\n      直接回答了 cost-benefit 问题：如果用户已经愿意花 Nx 推理成本做 sampling，\n      用 SJ 而非 logprob 做选择只增加 O(N²) 的 CPU 计算（<1% 的推理成本），\n      但额外获得 1.2-2.5pp F1。这是 \"free lunch\" 论点的核心。\n\n  - name: ner_ood_robustness\n    plan_id: exp-011\n    description: >\n      OOD 测试：用 WNUT-17 fine-tuned model 在 CoNLL-2003 test set 上做 NER inference，\n      或反之。测试 SJ 信号在 domain shift 下的鲁棒性。\n    expected_results:\n      ood_greedy_f1: 0.42\n      ood_oracle_f1: 0.58\n      ood_headroom: 0.16\n      ood_sj_rho: 0.33\n      ood_fk_rho: 0.24\n      ood_logprob_rho: 0.21\n      ood_sj_beats_logprob: true\n      ood_sj_minus_logprob: 0.12\n      ood_sj_bestofn_f1: 0.455\n      ood_sj_over_greedy: 3.5\n      n: 1287\n    result_rationale: >\n      OOD 下 greedy F1 大幅下降（从 in-domain 的 ~0.55-0.72 降至 ~0.42），\n      反映 domain shift 导致 model 能力退化。\n      SJ ρ=0.33 也低于 in-domain（0.37-0.42），但 SJ 仍是最佳信号且仍显著优于 logprob（Δ=0.12）。\n      这一结果有重要的实用意义：在 real-world 部署中，model 经常面对 distribution shift，\n      此时 logprob 因为 model miscalibration（在 OOD data 上 overconfident）而特别不可靠，\n      而 SJ 因为直接度量 output 间的 structural agreement 而更鲁棒——\n      如果 model 在 OOD instance 上不确定，它的 samples 自然会不一致，SJ 会低；\n      如果它碰巧在某个 OOD instance 上仍然一致地正确，SJ 会高。\n      这种 \"behavior-based\" vs \"probability-based\" 的差异在 OOD 下尤为突出。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: In-domain vs OOD signal comparison\"\n        columns: [Setting, Greedy_F1, SJ_rho, FK_rho, Logprob_rho, SJ-Logprob]\n        rows:\n          - [In-domain (WNUT), 0.541, 0.37, 0.28, 0.22, +0.15]\n          - [OOD (WNUT→CoNLL), 0.42, 0.33, 0.24, 0.21, +0.12]\n          - [Delta, -0.121, -0.04, -0.04, -0.01, -0.03]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"In-domain vs OOD bar chart: 展示所有信号在两种 setting 下的 ρ，SJ 的退化幅度最小（-0.04 vs logprob 的 -0.01，但 SJ 的绝对水平始终更高）。\"\n    analysis: >\n      OOD 结果是 appendix material 而非 main body，但为 robustness 提供了额外支撑。\n      SJ 在 OOD 下的优势（+0.12 over logprob）甚至比 logprob 自身的 in-domain 值（0.22）的\n      一半还多，说明在实际部署场景中 SJ 的价值更大。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14366,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14366},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72634f08-10d3-4aa1-9d4e-f87016e5fcde","uuid":"505e6e89-694a-48e3-b2e4-073f33672927"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":548901,"duration_api_ms":550160,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  原始 framing 完全成立。SJ 在所有 NER 场景下显著优于全部 baseline（含 log-prob），\n  Δρ ≥ 0.12 证明结构一致性捕获了模型置信度之外的互补信息。\n  16x 推理成本通过 best-of-N F1 提升得到正当性（+4.5pp over greedy, +2.5pp over logprob）。\n  Cross-dataset（CoNLL, WNUT）和 cross-model（LLaMA）均复现排序 SJ > FK > entity-voting > logprob > exact-match。\n  RE 诊断故事自然成立：所有信号在 RE full 上均退化至 ρ<0.25，compound error propagation 是普遍瓶颈而非 SJ 特有缺陷。\n  AUROC/τ/calibration 多指标一致确认 SJ 最优，leave-one-out 排除评估循环性。\n  目标 EMNLP Main，contribution = systematic comparison + diagnostic framework。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: baseline_logprob\n    plan_id: exp-012\n    description: >\n      对 pilot_005（SciERC NER+RE, N=8, T=0.7）样本做 vLLM forward pass 提取 sequence log-prob，\n      计算 instance-level mean log-prob 与 greedy F1 的 Spearman ρ。\n    expected_results:\n      scierc_ner_logprob_rho: 0.24\n      scierc_ner_logprob_p: 2.1e-8\n      scierc_ner_sj_minus_logprob: 0.148\n      scierc_re_full_logprob_rho: 0.22\n      scierc_re_cond_logprob_rho: 0.30\n      scierc_re_cond_sj_minus_logprob: 0.072\n      n_ner: 529\n      n_re_full: 397\n      n_re_cond: 301\n    result_rationale: >\n      Sequence log-prob 是 token-level 概率的聚合，包含格式 token、类型标签、结构标记等的贡献，\n      对单个实体正确性的区分度被稀释。一个高 log-prob 序列可能因大部分 token 是确定性格式输出\n      而得分高，但某个实体 span 仍然错误；反之，正确识别了罕见实体的序列可能因实体本身低频而\n      拉低整体 log-prob。SJ 直接在实体集合层面度量结构重叠，信号更具针对性。\n      NER 上 Δρ=0.148 远超 0.08 阈值，证明 structural consistency 捕获了 model confidence 之外的信息。\n      RE full 上 logprob（0.22）与 SJ（0.234）几乎持平，因为 compound error 同时摧毁了两类信号的区分力；\n      RE cond 上 logprob（0.30）仍低于 SJ（0.372），说明在模型能力范围内结构信号仍有优势。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Log-prob vs SJ/FK correlation (pilot_005, SciERC)\"\n        columns: [Task, Subset, SJ_rho, FK_rho, Logprob_rho, SJ_minus_Logprob]\n        rows:\n          - [NER, full, 0.3875, 0.3211, 0.24, +0.148]\n          - [NER, conditional, 0.3868, 0.3050, 0.23, +0.157]\n          - [RE, full, 0.2343, 0.1835, 0.22, +0.014]\n          - [RE, conditional, 0.3716, 0.2533, 0.30, +0.072]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: instance-level mean logprob vs greedy F1 (NER), 与 SJ vs F1 scatter 并排比较。SJ scatter 更紧密地沿对角线分布，logprob scatter 明显更散。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Make-or-break 实验通过：SJ 在 NER 上以 Δρ=0.148 显著优于 logprob，证明 16x 推理成本\n      换来的结构一致性信号包含 model confidence 之外的互补信息。关键洞察：logprob 是 sequence-level\n      信号，在实体数量 ≥3 的实例上尤其退化（这些实例的 logprob 被高频格式 token 主导），\n      而 SJ 的 set-level 比较在这些实例上反而表现更好。RE 上两者收敛说明 compound error 是\n      共同瓶颈，不是 SJ 特有问题。\n\n  - name: baseline_exact_match\n    plan_id: exp-013\n    description: >\n      对 pilot_005 existing data 计算 exact-match voting rate：N=8 samples 中产生完全相同\n      entity/relation set 的比例。Correlate with F1。\n    expected_results:\n      scierc_ner_exact_match_rho: 0.19\n      scierc_ner_exact_match_p: 1.4e-5\n      scierc_ner_mean_exact_match_rate: 0.06\n      scierc_re_full_exact_match_rho: 0.13\n      scierc_re_full_mean_exact_match_rate: 0.02\n      n_ner: 529\n      n_re: 397\n    result_rationale: >\n      Exact-match 对结构化输出过于严格：改变一个 entity span boundary（如 \"neural network\" vs\n      \"neural networks\"）即判定两个 sample 完全不同。N=8 且 T=0.7 下，NER 平均 exact-match rate\n      仅 ~6%（每个 instance 平均 0.5 对 sample 完全相同），导致信号极度稀疏和噪声化。\n      大多数 instance 的 exact-match rate 为 0 或接近 0，区分力很差。\n      这正是 Wang et al. (2023) 的 self-consistency 方法直接应用于结构化输出时的核心局限：\n      该方法为推理任务设计，输出空间小且离散（如数字答案），对结构化输出不适用。\n      RE 更差（mean rate ~2%），因为 relation triple 的组合空间远大于 entity set。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Exact-match statistics (pilot_005)\"\n        columns: [Task, Mean_EM_Rate, Median_EM_Rate, Pct_Zero_EM, rho_with_F1]\n        rows:\n          - [NER, 0.06, 0.04, 68.2, 0.19]\n          - [RE, 0.02, 0.00, 87.4, 0.13]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Histogram: exact-match rate 分布（NER/RE），展示大部分 instance EM rate 集中在 0 附近，少数 instance 有非零 EM。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Exact-match 是最弱的 baseline，ρ=0.19 远低于 SJ（0.39）。该结果从理论上预期且必要：\n      它量化了 structured output 与 flat answer 的根本差异，justifies 为何 set-aware metric\n      对 IE self-consistency 不可或缺。论文中这是 \"为什么需要 soft matching\" 的实证支撑。\n\n  - name: baseline_entity_voting\n    plan_id: exp-014\n    description: >\n      Entity-level majority voting：统计每个 entity 在 N=8 samples 中出现的频率，\n      选择出现频率 > threshold 的 entities 构成 voted set。比较 voted-set F1 与\n      SJ-selected sample F1。同时计算 instance-level voting confidence（mean entity frequency）\n      与 F1 的相关性。\n    expected_results:\n      scierc_ner_entity_voting_rho: 0.29\n      scierc_ner_entity_voting_p: 3.7e-12\n      scierc_ner_voted_set_f1_at_threshold_0.5: 0.694\n      scierc_ner_voted_set_f1_at_threshold_0.375: 0.701\n      scierc_ner_voted_set_f1_at_threshold_0.625: 0.682\n      scierc_ner_sj_selected_f1: 0.698\n      n_ner: 529\n    result_rationale: >\n      Entity voting 比 exact-match 和 logprob 更强（ρ=0.29），因为它在 entity 粒度操作，\n      与 F1 的评估粒度一致。但它仍弱于 SJ（0.39），原因有二：\n      (1) Entity voting 独立处理每个 entity，忽略了 entity 间的共现结构——如果 entity A 和 B\n      倾向于一起出现或不出现，SJ 的 pairwise set comparison 能捕获这种耦合，voting 不能。\n      (2) Entity voting 构造一个 \"合成\" 的 voted set，这个 set 可能不对应任何一个实际 sample，\n      存在 Frankenstein 效应（组合了来自不同 sample 的 entity）。SJ 选择的是一个真实 sample，\n      保持了内部一致性。\n      Voted-set F1（0.694-0.701）与 SJ-selected F1（0.698）接近，但 SJ 的优势在于\n      它同时提供了可靠的 confidence ranking（用于选择和 calibration），而 entity voting\n      只能在固定 threshold 下产生单一输出。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Entity voting vs SJ selection (NER, pilot_005)\"\n        columns: [Method, F1, Confidence_rho, Note]\n        rows:\n          - [Greedy, 0.662, \"—\", \"T=0 baseline\"]\n          - [Entity_voting_t0.5, 0.694, 0.29, \"threshold=0.5\"]\n          - [Entity_voting_t0.375, 0.701, 0.29, \"optimal threshold\"]\n          - [SJ_selection, 0.698, 0.39, \"select max-SJ sample\"]\n          - [Oracle, 0.759, \"—\", \"best of N=8\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: F1 of greedy vs entity-voting (multiple thresholds) vs SJ-selected vs oracle，展示各方法在 headroom 中的位置。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Entity voting 是最强的非-SJ baseline（ρ=0.29），但 SJ 仍以 Δρ=0.10 显著领先。\n      Entity voting 的 voted-set F1 与 SJ-selected F1 接近的事实并不削弱 SJ 的贡献，\n      因为 SJ 提供了连续的 confidence score 可用于 ranking/calibration/selection，\n      而 entity voting 在每个 threshold 下只产生一个输出。\n      论文中 entity voting 作为 \"entity-level baseline\" 占据 FK 和 logprob 之间的位置，\n      强化了 \"需要 set-level structural comparison\" 的论点。\n\n  - name: evaluation_metrics_expansion\n    plan_id: exp-015\n    description: >\n      对所有 confidence signals (SJ, FK, logprob, exact-match, entity-voting) 在所有数据集上\n      计算 AUROC、Kendall τ、ECE calibration、leave-one-out SJ。\n    expected_results:\n      scierc_ner_sj_auroc: 0.75\n      scierc_ner_sj_tau: 0.31\n      scierc_ner_sj_ece: 0.08\n      scierc_ner_fk_auroc: 0.68\n      scierc_ner_fk_tau: 0.24\n      scierc_ner_fk_ece: 0.12\n      scierc_ner_logprob_auroc: 0.63\n      scierc_ner_logprob_tau: 0.18\n      scierc_ner_logprob_ece: 0.15\n      scierc_ner_exact_match_auroc: 0.58\n      scierc_ner_exact_match_tau: 0.14\n      scierc_ner_entity_voting_auroc: 0.66\n      scierc_ner_entity_voting_tau: 0.22\n      scierc_ner_leave_one_out_sj_rho: 0.40\n      scierc_ner_leave_one_out_sj_auroc: 0.74\n      conll_ner_sj_auroc: 0.74\n      conll_ner_sj_tau: 0.30\n      wnut_ner_sj_auroc: 0.71\n      wnut_ner_sj_tau: 0.27\n      re_full_sj_auroc: 0.58\n      re_full_logprob_auroc: 0.57\n      re_cond_sj_auroc: 0.69\n    result_rationale: >\n      AUROC（二分类：F1 > median 为 \"good\"）和 Kendall τ（rank correlation）与 Spearman ρ\n      度量不同方面的信号质量：AUROC 测量二值区分能力，τ 对 tied ranks 更鲁棒。\n      在 best 档位下，三个 rank-based 指标（ρ, τ, AUROC）的排序完全一致：SJ > FK > entity-voting > logprob > exact-match。\n      这排除了\"SJ 仅在某个特定指标上偶然胜出\"的可能性。\n      ECE（Expected Calibration Error）揭示 SJ 的校准优势：SJ score 的值域（0-1）天然对应\n      \"置信度\"语义，高 SJ 意味着 samples 高度一致，低 SJ 意味着分歧大。Logprob 的 ECE 更高\n      因为 LLM 倾向于 overconfident（高 logprob 不代表高 accuracy）。\n      Leave-one-out SJ（ρ=0.40 vs full SJ ρ=0.42）仅下降 0.02，证明评估无循环性：\n      SJ signal 不依赖于 \"被评估 sample 自身参与 SJ 计算\" 才有效。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Multi-metric comparison (SciERC NER, N=16)\"\n        columns: [Signal, Spearman_rho, Kendall_tau, AUROC, ECE]\n        rows:\n          - [SJ, 0.42, 0.31, 0.75, 0.08]\n          - [FK, 0.33, 0.24, 0.68, 0.12]\n          - [Entity_voting, 0.30, 0.22, 0.66, 0.11]\n          - [Logprob, 0.26, 0.18, 0.63, 0.15]\n          - [Exact_match, 0.20, 0.14, 0.58, 0.19]\n          - [Leave-one-out_SJ, 0.40, 0.29, 0.74, 0.09]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Calibration plot（5 panels）：每个 signal 的 predicted confidence bin vs observed accuracy。SJ 接近对角线（ECE=0.08），logprob 系统性偏高（overconfident）。\"\n      - \"Radar chart：5 signals × 4 metrics（ρ, τ, AUROC, 1-ECE），SJ 在所有维度上最大。\"\n    analysis: >\n      多指标一致性是论文 robustness 的关键支撑。Leave-one-out SJ 仅微降 0.02 直接化解\n      R9 circularity 质疑。ECE 分析额外揭示了 SJ 作为 calibrated confidence 的实用价值——\n      不仅排序最好，而且校准最好，可直接用于 selective prediction 等下游应用。\n\n  - name: ner_n16_scierc\n    plan_id: exp-001\n    description: >\n      SciERC NER N=16（ft_002_v2），T=0.7，seeds=[42, 123, 456]。\n      增强 ρ 估计稳定性，验证 N-scaling 效应。Inference 同时捕获 log-prob。\n    expected_results:\n      ner_greedy_f1: 0.662\n      ner_oracle_f1_n16: 0.797\n      ner_headroom_n16: 0.135\n      ner_sj_rho_seed42: 0.41\n      ner_sj_rho_seed123: 0.43\n      ner_sj_rho_seed456: 0.42\n      ner_sj_rho_mean: 0.42\n      ner_sj_rho_std: 0.01\n      ner_fk_rho_mean: 0.33\n      ner_fk_rho_std: 0.012\n      ner_logprob_rho_mean: 0.26\n      ner_sj_minus_fk_mean: 0.09\n      ner_sj_minus_logprob_mean: 0.16\n      ner_sj_p_mean: 1.8e-24\n      ner_sample_f1_mean: 0.628\n      ner_sample_f1_std: 0.308\n      ner_sample_f1_pct_zero: 10.5\n      n: 529\n    result_rationale: >\n      从 N=8（ρ=0.388）到 N=16（ρ=0.42）的提升来自 SJ 估计的统计稳定性：\n      pairwise comparisons 从 C(8,2)=28 增至 C(16,2)=120，mean SJ 的方差降低约 4x。\n      对于 \"边缘\" instance（SJ 在 N=8 时估计噪声大），N=16 下 SJ 更准确地反映真实一致性水平，\n      减少了 ranking noise，因此 ρ 上升。FK 的改善较小（+0.01）因为 FK 作为单一标量已在 N=8\n      时就比较稳定。Logprob 也改善至 0.26（更多 sample 的 mean logprob 更稳定），但绝对水平\n      仍远低于 SJ。\n      Oracle F1 从 0.759（N=8）升至 0.797（N=16），headroom 从 0.097 升至 0.135，\n      证明更多 sample 确实产生更好的候选，为 best-of-N 提供更大改进空间。\n      三个 seed 的 std=0.01 表明结果高度稳定，非 random seed 的偶然。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: N=8 vs N=16 comparison (SciERC NER)\"\n        columns: [N, SJ_rho, FK_rho, Logprob_rho, Oracle_F1, Headroom]\n        rows:\n          - [8, 0.388, 0.321, 0.24, 0.759, 0.097]\n          - [16, 0.42, 0.33, 0.26, 0.797, 0.135]\n          - [Delta, +0.032, +0.009, +0.02, +0.038, +0.038]\n      - title: \"Table: Multi-seed robustness (N=16)\"\n        columns: [Seed, SJ_rho, FK_rho, SJ_p]\n        rows:\n          - [42, 0.41, 0.32, 2.8e-23]\n          - [123, 0.43, 0.34, 4.1e-25]\n          - [456, 0.42, 0.33, 1.2e-24]\n          - [Mean±Std, \"0.42±0.01\", \"0.33±0.01\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"SJ ρ 随 N scaling 的折线图（N=2,4,8,16），展示 SJ ρ 单调递增且在 N=16 时尚未饱和，暗示更多 sample 仍能改善。\"\n    analysis: >\n      N=16 将 SJ ρ 推入 [0.39, 0.45] 的 best 范围，multi-seed std=0.01 表明这不是随机波动。\n      SJ 从 N-scaling 中获益最大这一事实本身就是证据：SJ 是一个需要充分 pairwise comparison\n      才能发挥潜力的信号，这与其 set-level structural comparison 的设计一致。\n      Headroom 增至 0.135 为 exp-006（best-of-N）的 F1 提升提供了上限。\n\n  - name: ner_conll2003\n    plan_id: exp-002\n    description: >\n      Fine-tune Qwen3-8B on CoNLL-2003（LoRA），NER pilot N=8, T=0.7。\n      Cross-dataset 泛化验证。\n    expected_results:\n      finetune_ner_f1: 0.724\n      finetune_train_loss: 0.065\n      ner_greedy_f1: 0.718\n      ner_oracle_f1: 0.815\n      ner_headroom: 0.097\n      ner_sj_rho: 0.41\n      ner_sj_p: 4.2e-38\n      ner_fk_rho: 0.31\n      ner_logprob_rho: 0.25\n      ner_exact_match_rho: 0.21\n      ner_entity_voting_rho: 0.30\n      ner_sj_minus_logprob: 0.16\n      ner_sample_f1_mean: 0.682\n      ner_sample_f1_pct_zero: 6.3\n      n: 3453\n    result_rationale: >\n      CoNLL-2003 是标准 NER benchmark（新闻文本，4 类 entity），Qwen3-8B + LoRA 应达到\n      ~72% F1（该数据集更大、更干净，entity 类型更规范）。因为 model 在 CoNLL 上基础能力\n      更强（F1 从 SciERC 的 0.66 升至 0.72），sample 间一致性更高（mean SJ 更高），\n      但 SJ 仍能有效区分 \"一致正确\" 和 \"一致但错误/不一致\" 的 instance。\n      SJ ρ=0.41 与 SciERC 的 0.42 接近，说明 SJ 的有效性不依赖于特定 domain 或 entity schema。\n      Logprob ρ=0.25 同样接近 SciERC 上的 0.24-0.26，排序 SJ > FK > entity-voting > logprob > exact-match\n      完全复现。\n      Sample F1 pct_zero 降至 6.3%（SciERC 为 10.5%），反映 CoNLL 的更高 model competence。\n      N 从 529 升至 3453（CoNLL test set 更大），给出更强的统计功效（p 值更小）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Cross-dataset signal comparison (N=8)\"\n        columns: [Dataset, SJ_rho, FK_rho, Logprob_rho, EM_rho, EV_rho, N]\n        rows:\n          - [SciERC, 0.388, 0.321, 0.24, 0.19, 0.29, 529]\n          - [CoNLL-2003, 0.41, 0.31, 0.25, 0.21, 0.30, 3453]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: 5 signals 在 SciERC 和 CoNLL 上的 ρ 并排比较，展示 ranking 一致性。\"\n    analysis: >\n      CoNLL 复现了 SciERC 上的信号排序，且在更大 test set 上具有更强统计功效。\n      Domain 从科学论文切换到新闻文本，entity schema 从 6 类（SciERC）切换到 4 类（CoNLL），\n      SJ 优势不变，证明了 domain-agnostic 性质。\n\n  - name: ner_wnut17\n    plan_id: exp-003\n    description: >\n      Fine-tune Qwen3-8B on WNUT-17（LoRA），NER pilot N=8, T=0.7。\n      社交媒体域——噪声文本的 cross-dataset 泛化。\n    expected_results:\n      finetune_ner_f1: 0.548\n      ner_greedy_f1: 0.541\n      ner_oracle_f1: 0.695\n      ner_headroom: 0.154\n      ner_sj_rho: 0.37\n      ner_sj_p: 3.1e-12\n      ner_fk_rho: 0.28\n      ner_logprob_rho: 0.22\n      ner_exact_match_rho: 0.17\n      ner_entity_voting_rho: 0.27\n      ner_sj_minus_logprob: 0.15\n      ner_sample_f1_mean: 0.468\n      ner_sample_f1_pct_zero: 22.8\n      n: 1287\n    result_rationale: >\n      WNUT-17 是最具挑战性的 NER 数据集（社交媒体、emerging entities、noisy text），\n      greedy F1 ~54% 反映任务难度。更大的 headroom（0.154）说明 model 的不确定性更高，\n      stochastic samples 间差异更大。\n      SJ ρ=0.37 是三个数据集中最低的，但仍在 best 范围 [0.33, 0.42] 内。原因：\n      (1) 噪声文本导致 entity span 在 samples 间变化更大（如缩写、拼写变体），\n      SJ 的 soft matching 能容忍这些变化但信号本身不如干净文本上清晰；\n      (2) emerging entity 类型本身定义模糊，model 对同一 mention 可能分配不同 type，\n      降低了 SJ 的区分力。\n      尽管如此，SJ 仍以 Δρ=0.15 显著优于 logprob，排序完全保持。\n      Sample F1 pct_zero=22.8% 是最高的，反映 model 在社交媒体文本上更频繁地生成空或全错输出。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: WNUT-17 signal comparison\"\n        columns: [Signal, rho, p_value, rho_rank]\n        rows:\n          - [SJ, 0.37, 3.1e-12, 1]\n          - [FK, 0.28, 8.5e-7, 2]\n          - [Entity_voting, 0.27, 2.1e-6, 3]\n          - [Logprob, 0.22, 4.7e-4, 4]\n          - [Exact_match, 0.17, 6.2e-3, 5]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-dataset ρ comparison heatmap: rows=datasets (SciERC, CoNLL, WNUT), columns=signals, color=ρ magnitude. 所有行的 ranking 一致。\"\n    analysis: >\n      WNUT 是 \"stress test\"：最难的 domain、最低的 model 能力。SJ 仍胜出但 margin 比\n      CoNLL/SciERC 略小，符合预期——更低的基础性能意味着 samples 间差异更大、SJ 估计更 noisy。\n      关键是排序不变，证明 SJ 的优势是 structural 而非 domain-specific。\n\n  - name: re_diagnostic_analysis\n    plan_id: exp-004\n    description: >\n      SciERC RE 的深度诊断：per-relation-type breakdown、所有信号的 bootstrap CI、\n      conditional threshold sensitivity analysis。\n    expected_results:\n      re_full_sj_rho: 0.234\n      re_full_sj_rho_ci95: [0.14, 0.33]\n      re_full_fk_rho: 0.184\n      re_full_fk_rho_ci95: [0.09, 0.28]\n      re_full_logprob_rho: 0.22\n      re_full_logprob_rho_ci95: [0.12, 0.31]\n      re_full_exact_match_rho: 0.13\n      re_full_exact_match_rho_ci95: [0.03, 0.23]\n      re_cond_sj_rho: 0.39\n      re_cond_sj_rho_ci95: [0.29, 0.48]\n      re_cond_fk_rho: 0.25\n      re_cond_logprob_rho: 0.30\n      per_relation_type_rho_sj_Used_for: 0.28\n      per_relation_type_rho_sj_Feature_of: 0.22\n      per_relation_type_rho_sj_Hyponym_of: 0.19\n      per_relation_type_rho_sj_Part_of: 0.24\n      per_relation_type_rho_sj_Compare: 0.17\n      per_relation_type_rho_sj_Evaluate_for: 0.15\n      threshold_sensitivity_t0.3_cond_n: 365\n      threshold_sensitivity_t0.3_cond_sj_rho: 0.32\n      threshold_sensitivity_t0.5_cond_n: 340\n      threshold_sensitivity_t0.5_cond_sj_rho: 0.35\n      threshold_sensitivity_t0.7_cond_n: 301\n      threshold_sensitivity_t0.7_cond_sj_rho: 0.39\n      threshold_sensitivity_t0.9_cond_n: 248\n      threshold_sensitivity_t0.9_cond_sj_rho: 0.44\n      n_full: 397\n    result_rationale: >\n      Per-relation-type 分析揭示所有 relation type 的 SJ ρ 都远低于 NER 水平（0.15-0.28），\n      且频率最高的 Used-for（占 ~40% relations）反而不是最好的——这排除了\"某些 rare type 拉低平均值\"\n      的 cherry-pick 质疑。所有 type 都受 compound error 影响：一个 relation 的正确性同时依赖\n      head entity span、tail entity span、relation type 三个组件，任一出错即导致 F1=0。\n      这解释了为什么 e1_component_wise_re_sj 中 head_sj ρ=0.210 远低于 NER ρ=0.383——\n      不是 span-level SJ 失效，而是 RE 的 entity extraction 本身就不如独立 NER 任务准确\n      （joint extraction 的 multi-task 干扰）。\n      Bootstrap CI 显示 NER SJ ρ 的 95% CI 下界（~0.33）仍高于 RE SJ ρ 的上界（~0.33），\n      确认 NER-RE gap 是统计显著的。\n      Threshold sensitivity 分析展示 conditional ρ 随 threshold 单调递增（从 0.32 到 0.44），\n      证明 T=0.7 的选择不是 cherry-pick 而是 principled 的：随着排除更多 knowledge-gap instance，\n      信号持续改善。但 N 同时下降（365→248），存在 power-quality tradeoff。\n      关键发现：logprob 在 RE cond 上（ρ=0.30）与 FK（ρ=0.25）接近且都远低于 SJ（ρ=0.39），\n      说明即使 compound error 削弱了所有信号，SJ 在模型能力范围内仍最好。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: RE per-relation-type SJ ρ\"\n        columns: [Relation_Type, Frequency, SJ_rho, FK_rho, N]\n        rows:\n          - [Used-for, 0.39, 0.28, 0.20, 155]\n          - [Feature-of, 0.17, 0.22, 0.16, 67]\n          - [Part-of, 0.13, 0.24, 0.19, 52]\n          - [Hyponym-of, 0.12, 0.19, 0.14, 48]\n          - [Compare, 0.11, 0.17, 0.12, 44]\n          - [Evaluate-for, 0.08, 0.15, 0.11, 31]\n      - title: \"Table: Conditional threshold sensitivity (RE, SJ)\"\n        columns: [Threshold, N_cond, SJ_rho, FK_rho, Logprob_rho]\n        rows:\n          - [0.0 (full), 397, 0.234, 0.184, 0.22]\n          - [0.3, 365, 0.32, 0.22, 0.26]\n          - [0.5, 340, 0.35, 0.24, 0.28]\n          - [0.7, 301, 0.39, 0.25, 0.30]\n          - [0.9, 248, 0.44, 0.29, 0.34]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Threshold sensitivity curve: x=threshold, y=SJ ρ，左 y-axis 标 ρ，右 y-axis 标 conditional N，展示 quality-power tradeoff。\"\n      - \"Per-relation-type grouped bar chart，对比 NER entity-type ρ（稳定在 0.35-0.45）和 RE relation-type ρ（全部 <0.30），视觉化 compound error 的冲击。\"\n    analysis: >\n      诊断分析完整支撑 Claim 2：compound error propagation 是 RE 上所有信号退化的共同原因，\n      而非 SJ 特有缺陷。Per-type 分析证明没有任何 relation type 能达到 NER 水平的信号质量。\n      Threshold sensitivity 的单调递增排除了 cherry-pick 质疑——T=0.7 是 coverage/quality 平衡点，\n      不是精心挑选的。Bootstrap CI 给出严格的统计推断基础。\n\n  - name: temperature_sensitivity_analysis\n    plan_id: exp-005\n    description: >\n      T=0.7（pilot_005）vs T=1.0（pilot_004）的 signal-noise tradeoff 分析，\n      涵盖所有 confidence signals。\n    expected_results:\n      ner_t07_sj_rho: 0.3875\n      ner_t10_sj_rho: 0.3825\n      ner_t07_fk_rho: 0.3211\n      ner_t10_fk_rho: 0.2590\n      ner_t07_logprob_rho: 0.23\n      ner_t10_logprob_rho: 0.26\n      ner_t07_exact_match_rho: 0.20\n      ner_t10_exact_match_rho: 0.15\n      re_t07_sj_rho: 0.2343\n      re_t10_sj_rho: 0.2441\n      re_t07_logprob_rho: 0.21\n      re_t10_logprob_rho: 0.24\n      mean_sj_t07: 0.776\n      mean_sj_t10: 0.701\n      mean_fk_t07: 0.472\n      mean_fk_t10: 0.405\n    result_rationale: >\n      T=0.7 vs T=1.0 的 tradeoff：\n      - SJ 在 T=0.7 更好（+0.005 NER）：T=0.7 下 samples 更接近 model 的 mode，\n        SJ 的 pairwise overlap 更高（mean SJ 0.776 vs 0.701），但高 SJ 并不代表缺乏区分力——\n        instance 间的 relative ordering 在低噪声下更准确。\n      - FK 在 T=0.7 显著更好（+0.062 NER）：FK 对噪声更敏感，T=1.0 的高采样多样性\n        导致 FK 系统性偏低（因为 FK 惩罚任何不一致），掩盖了真实的 agreement 差异。\n      - Logprob 在 T=1.0 稍好（+0.03 NER）：T=1.0 下 logprob 值的 variance 更大\n        （序列多样性 → logprob 分布更宽），给出了更多排序信息。\n      - Exact-match 在 T=0.7 更好（+0.05 NER）：低温下更多 exact duplicate，EM rate 从\n        几乎全零变为可用信号。\n      关键洞察：SJ 是唯一在两个温度下都表现最好的信号，对 T 选择最鲁棒。\n      Logprob 是唯一在 T=1.0 优于 T=0.7 的信号，但即使在其最优温度下仍不如 SJ 在其最差温度下。\n      RE 上所有信号在两个温度下都差（ρ<0.25），T 选择对 RE 的影响不大，进一步支持\n      compound error 是 RE 的根本瓶颈而非 hyperparameter 问题。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Temperature × Signal interaction (NER)\"\n        columns: [Signal, T=0.7_rho, T=1.0_rho, Delta, Better_at]\n        rows:\n          - [SJ, 0.388, 0.383, +0.005, \"T=0.7\"]\n          - [FK, 0.321, 0.259, +0.062, \"T=0.7\"]\n          - [Logprob, 0.23, 0.26, -0.03, \"T=1.0\"]\n          - [Exact_match, 0.20, 0.15, +0.05, \"T=0.7\"]\n      - title: \"Table: Temperature × Signal interaction (RE full)\"\n        columns: [Signal, T=0.7_rho, T=1.0_rho, Delta]\n        rows:\n          - [SJ, 0.234, 0.244, -0.010]\n          - [FK, 0.184, 0.278, -0.094]\n          - [Logprob, 0.21, 0.24, -0.03]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: signal × temperature × task，color = ρ。NER 行中 SJ 在两个 T 下都最深色；RE 行全浅色。\"\n      - \"Signal-noise tradeoff 概念图：x=sampling diversity (T), y=signal quality (ρ)，SJ 曲线最平（最鲁棒），FK 曲线最陡（对 T 最敏感）。\"\n    analysis: >\n      温度分析的核心贡献不是\"推荐 T=0.7\"，而是揭示 SJ 对 temperature 的鲁棒性。\n      SJ 在 T=0.7 和 T=1.0 下的 ρ 差异仅 0.005（NER），而 FK 的差异高达 0.062。\n      这意味着 SJ 在实际部署中不需要精细的 temperature tuning，降低了实用门槛。\n      Logprob 在 T=1.0 更好这一反直觉发现值得在论文中突出——它说明 logprob 和 consistency\n      signals 受 temperature 的影响方向相反，进一步证明两者捕获了不同类型的信息。\n\n  - name: adaptive_compute_demo\n    plan_id: exp-006\n    description: >\n      Best-of-N selection 实战：SJ vs logprob vs FK vs exact-match vs entity-voting vs random vs greedy。\n      覆盖所有 NER 数据集 + RE。\n    expected_results:\n      scierc_ner_greedy_f1: 0.662\n      scierc_ner_random_f1: 0.668\n      scierc_ner_exact_match_f1: 0.680\n      scierc_ner_logprob_f1: 0.687\n      scierc_ner_entity_voting_f1: 0.695\n      scierc_ner_fk_f1: 0.698\n      scierc_ner_sj_f1: 0.712\n      scierc_ner_oracle_f1: 0.797\n      scierc_ner_sj_over_greedy: 5.0\n      scierc_ner_sj_over_logprob: 2.5\n      conll_ner_greedy_f1: 0.718\n      conll_ner_sj_f1: 0.756\n      conll_ner_logprob_f1: 0.734\n      conll_ner_sj_over_greedy: 3.8\n      conll_ner_sj_over_logprob: 2.2\n      wnut_ner_greedy_f1: 0.541\n      wnut_ner_sj_f1: 0.586\n      wnut_ner_logprob_f1: 0.563\n      wnut_ner_sj_over_greedy: 4.5\n      wnut_ner_sj_over_logprob: 2.3\n      re_full_greedy_f1: 0.422\n      re_full_sj_f1: 0.436\n      re_full_logprob_f1: 0.433\n      re_full_sj_over_greedy: 1.4\n      re_full_sj_over_logprob: 0.3\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best-of-N 将 confidence ranking 转化为实际 F1 提升。在 SciERC NER（N=16）上，\n      SJ 选择比 greedy 提升 +5.0pp F1，比 logprob 提升 +2.5pp。\n      提升机制：SJ 选择的 sample 是\"与其他 sample 最结构相似的\"，这倾向于选择\n      model 最确定的输出。高 SJ 的 sample 通常包含了 majority samples 同意的 entities，\n      排除了个别 sample 的 hallucination 或遗漏。\n      SJ 在所有三个 NER 数据集上都是最佳选择方法（SciERC +5.0pp, CoNLL +3.8pp, WNUT +4.5pp over greedy），\n      且 SJ 相对 logprob 的优势在所有数据集上 ≥2.2pp（在 best 范围 [1.5, 4.0] 内）。\n      CoNLL 上 SJ-over-greedy 最小（3.8pp）因为 greedy F1 最高（0.718），headroom 最小。\n      WNUT 上 SJ-over-greedy 中等（4.5pp），headroom 最大但信号 noisier。\n      RE 上 SJ 选择仅比 greedy 好 +1.4pp，且与 logprob 几乎无差（+0.3pp），\n      与 correlation 分析一致：信号质量差导致选择效果差。这是 honest 的 negative result，\n      增强了论文的可信度。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Best-of-N selection F1 across datasets and methods\"\n        columns: [Dataset, Greedy, Random, EM, Logprob, EV, FK, SJ, Oracle]\n        rows:\n          - [SciERC_NER, 0.662, 0.668, 0.680, 0.687, 0.695, 0.698, 0.712, 0.797]\n          - [CoNLL_NER, 0.718, 0.722, 0.730, 0.734, 0.742, 0.744, 0.756, 0.815]\n          - [WNUT_NER, 0.541, 0.546, 0.555, 0.563, 0.570, 0.573, 0.586, 0.695]\n          - [SciERC_RE, 0.422, 0.425, 0.428, 0.433, 0.432, 0.431, 0.436, 0.553]\n      - title: \"Table: Pairwise F1 gains (pp)\"\n        columns: [Dataset, SJ-Greedy, SJ-Logprob, SJ-FK, Logprob-Greedy]\n        rows:\n          - [SciERC_NER, +5.0, +2.5, +1.4, +2.5]\n          - [CoNLL_NER, +3.8, +2.2, +1.2, +1.6]\n          - [WNUT_NER, +4.5, +2.3, +1.3, +2.2]\n          - [SciERC_RE, +1.4, +0.3, +0.5, +1.1]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: 每个数据集的 F1 by selection method，从 greedy（最低）到 oracle（最高），SJ 突出标注。\"\n      - \"Headroom utilization chart: (method_F1 - greedy_F1) / (oracle_F1 - greedy_F1) 百分比，SJ 在 NER 上利用 35-40% headroom，logprob 仅 18-22%。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Best-of-N 是论文的 \"practical payoff\" 实验。SJ 在三个 NER 数据集上一致提供最大 F1 提升，\n      且 SJ-over-logprob 的 +2.2-2.5pp 优势 justifies 了 16x 推理成本：在 NER 应用中\n      （如 biomedical NER、legal entity extraction），+2.5pp F1 是显著的实用改善。\n      RE 的 marginal gain 印证了 Claim 2 的诊断结论——一致性信号在高复杂度任务上的 TTS 收益有限。\n      这为论文提供了完整的 positive + diagnostic 故事。\n\n  - name: ner_multi_model\n    plan_id: exp-007\n    description: >\n      LLaMA-3.1-8B-Instruct 在 SciERC 上的 NER pilot（LoRA fine-tune + N=8, T=0.7），\n      验证 model-agnostic 性质。\n    expected_results:\n      finetune_ner_f1: 0.635\n      ner_greedy_f1: 0.629\n      ner_oracle_f1: 0.768\n      ner_headroom: 0.139\n      ner_sj_rho: 0.38\n      ner_sj_p: 1.5e-20\n      ner_fk_rho: 0.30\n      ner_logprob_rho: 0.23\n      ner_exact_match_rho: 0.18\n      ner_entity_voting_rho: 0.28\n      ner_sj_minus_logprob: 0.15\n      ner_sj_minus_fk: 0.08\n      llama_sj_beats_logprob: true\n      ner_sample_f1_mean: 0.574\n      ner_sample_f1_pct_zero: 15.2\n      n: 529\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLaMA-3.1-8B 的 NER greedy F1（~0.63）略低于 Qwen3-8B（0.66），\n      因为 Qwen3-8B 在结构化生成方面有 architecture-level 优势（更好的 instruction following）。\n      但 SJ ρ=0.38 仍在 best 范围 [0.33, 0.43] 内，且 SJ 仍显著优于 logprob（Δρ=0.15）。\n      这证明 SJ 的有效性不依赖于特定 model architecture 或 pretraining data：\n      无论底层 LLM 如何，structural consistency 都是比 model confidence 更好的质量信号。\n      LLaMA 的 headroom（0.139）比 Qwen（0.097 at N=8）更大，说明 LLaMA 在 stochastic\n      sampling 时变化更大——这反而给了 SJ 更多 \"空间\" 来区分好坏 sample。\n      SJ vs FK 的优势（+0.08）略小于 Qwen 上的（+0.09），但方向一致。\n      所有信号排序 SJ > FK > entity-voting > logprob > exact-match 完全复现。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Cross-model comparison (SciERC NER, N=8, T=0.7)\"\n        columns: [Model, Greedy_F1, SJ_rho, FK_rho, Logprob_rho, SJ-Logprob]\n        rows:\n          - [Qwen3-8B, 0.662, 0.388, 0.321, 0.24, +0.148]\n          - [LLaMA-3.1-8B, 0.629, 0.38, 0.30, 0.23, +0.15]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired comparison plot: Qwen vs LLaMA 在 5 个信号上的 ρ 对比，虚线连接同一信号的两个 model 值，展示高度平行（ranking 一致）。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-model 验证是 R2 的直接回应。LLaMA 的 SJ ρ=0.38 略低于 Qwen 的 0.39，\n      但差异不显著（bootstrap CI 重叠），且关键的 SJ > logprob 关系完全保持。\n      论文可以 claim \"model-agnostic\"：在 Qwen 和 LLaMA 两个不同 architecture 家族上，\n      structural consistency 均优于 model confidence。\n\n  - name: re_n16_confirmation\n    plan_id: exp-008\n    description: >\n      SciERC RE N=16，确认 negative finding 的统计功效。\n    expected_results:\n      re_greedy_f1: 0.422\n      re_oracle_f1_n16: 0.612\n      re_headroom_n16: 0.190\n      re_full_sj_rho_n16: 0.27\n      re_full_sj_rho_ci95: [0.18, 0.36]\n      re_full_fk_rho_n16: 0.21\n      re_full_logprob_rho_n16: 0.25\n      re_cond_sj_rho_n16: 0.40\n      re_cond_sj_rho_ci95: [0.30, 0.49]\n      re_cond_n16_n: 301\n      n_full: 397\n    result_rationale: >\n      RE N=16 的 SJ ρ 从 N=8 的 0.234 提升至 0.27，幅度远小于 NER 的提升\n      （NER: 0.388 → 0.42，Δ=+0.032；RE: 0.234 → 0.27，Δ=+0.036）。\n      更多 sample（C(16,2)=120 vs C(8,2)=28）使 SJ 估计更稳定，但 compound error 的\n      根本瓶颈不因 sample 数量增加而消除：如果 model 在某个 instance 上系统性地无法正确\n      提取 head entity，16 个 sample 和 8 个 sample 犯同样的错误。\n      RE full ρ=0.27 仍在 best 范围 [0.2, 0.3] 内且远低于 NER 的 0.42，\n      以更高统计功效确认了 NER-RE gap。\n      RE cond ρ=0.40 从 0.39 微升，确认 conditional analysis 的有效性：\n      在 model 有能力的 subset 上，SJ 在 RE 上也能达到有用的信号质量。\n      Bootstrap CI 确保这不是 noise——full 的 CI 上界（0.36）低于 NER full ρ（0.42），\n      而 cond 的 CI 下界（0.30）仍高于 full 的点估计（0.27）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: RE N=8 vs N=16 comparison\"\n        columns: [N, Full_SJ_rho, Full_FK_rho, Full_Logprob_rho, Cond_SJ_rho, Oracle_F1]\n        rows:\n          - [8, 0.234, 0.184, 0.22, 0.372, 0.553]\n          - [16, 0.27, 0.21, 0.25, 0.40, 0.612]\n          - [Delta, +0.036, +0.026, +0.03, +0.028, +0.059]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"NER vs RE 的 N-scaling 对比折线图：NER 的 SJ ρ 曲线陡峭上升，RE 的 SJ ρ 曲线平缓，visual 化 compound error bottleneck。\"\n    analysis: >\n      N=16 确认了 RE negative finding 不是 sample insufficiency 问题。\n      即使给予更多 sample，RE full ρ 仍卡在 0.27（NER 已达 0.42），\n      这是 \"diagnostic evidence\" 的核心：compound error 是 structural bottleneck，\n      不是 estimation noise。\n\n  - name: capability_stratification\n    plan_id: exp-009\n    description: >\n      按 greedy F1 bucket 和独立 proxy（sentence length, entity count）分层分析 SJ ρ，\n      验证 inverted-U pattern。\n    expected_results:\n      ner_f1_bucket_0_0.3_sj_rho: 0.12\n      ner_f1_bucket_0_0.3_n: 78\n      ner_f1_bucket_0.3_0.5_sj_rho: 0.35\n      ner_f1_bucket_0.3_0.5_n: 95\n      ner_f1_bucket_0.5_0.7_sj_rho: 0.48\n      ner_f1_bucket_0.5_0.7_n: 143\n      ner_f1_bucket_0.7_0.9_sj_rho: 0.39\n      ner_f1_bucket_0.7_0.9_n: 126\n      ner_f1_bucket_0.9_1.0_sj_rho: 0.22\n      ner_f1_bucket_0.9_1.0_n: 87\n      ner_sent_length_short_sj_rho: 0.40\n      ner_sent_length_short_n: 175\n      ner_sent_length_medium_sj_rho: 0.44\n      ner_sent_length_medium_n: 198\n      ner_sent_length_long_sj_rho: 0.36\n      ner_sent_length_long_n: 156\n      ner_entity_count_1_2_sj_rho: 0.45\n      ner_entity_count_1_2_n: 210\n      ner_entity_count_3_5_sj_rho: 0.41\n      ner_entity_count_3_5_n: 195\n      ner_entity_count_6plus_sj_rho: 0.34\n      ner_entity_count_6plus_n: 124\n      re_f1_bucket_0.5_0.7_sj_rho: 0.38\n      re_f1_bucket_0.5_0.7_n: 72\n    result_rationale: >\n      Greedy F1 bucket 分析显示 inverted-U pattern：\n      - F1=0-0.3（knowledge gap）：SJ ρ=0.12。Model 在这些 instance 上缺乏能力，\n        所有 sample 都差（一致地错），SJ 高但 F1 低，或 SJ 低但 F1 也低——没有区分力。\n      - F1=0.5-0.7（uncertainty region）：SJ ρ=0.48（峰值）。Model 有部分能力但不确定，\n        consistency 高低直接反映 output quality——这正是 self-consistency 最有价值的区间。\n      - F1=0.9-1.0（mastery）：SJ ρ=0.22。Model 几乎总是正确，SJ 一致地高，\n        ceiling effect 导致缺乏 variance 来建立 correlation。\n      独立 proxy（sentence length, entity count）验证了类似 pattern 但避免了\n      \"用 F1 分层再与 F1 相关\" 的循环性：\n      - Entity count 是最好的独立 proxy：1-2 entities 的 instance SJ ρ 最高（0.45），\n        因为这些 instance 的 \"uncertainty region\" 最清晰——每个 entity 的对错直接映射到 F1。\n      - 6+ entities 的 instance SJ ρ 下降（0.34），因为组合复杂度增加了噪声。\n      - Sentence length 的 pattern 较弱（medium 略好于 short/long），因为 length 与\n        task difficulty 的关系不单调。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: SJ ρ by greedy F1 bucket (NER, N=16)\"\n        columns: [F1_Bucket, N, SJ_rho, FK_rho, Logprob_rho]\n        rows:\n          - [\"[0, 0.3)\", 78, 0.12, 0.09, 0.14]\n          - [\"[0.3, 0.5)\", 95, 0.35, 0.26, 0.22]\n          - [\"[0.5, 0.7)\", 143, 0.48, 0.37, 0.29]\n          - [\"[0.7, 0.9)\", 126, 0.39, 0.31, 0.26]\n          - [\"[0.9, 1.0]\", 87, 0.22, 0.18, 0.15]\n      - title: \"Table: SJ ρ by independent proxy (NER, N=16)\"\n        columns: [Proxy, Stratum, N, SJ_rho]\n        rows:\n          - [Entity_count, \"1-2\", 210, 0.45]\n          - [Entity_count, \"3-5\", 195, 0.41]\n          - [Entity_count, \"6+\", 124, 0.34]\n          - [Sent_length, \"≤15 tok\", 175, 0.40]\n          - [Sent_length, \"16-30 tok\", 198, 0.44]\n          - [Sent_length, \">30 tok\", 156, 0.36]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Inverted-U curve: x=greedy F1 bucket midpoint, y=SJ ρ，peak 在 0.5-0.7 区间，清晰展示 uncertainty region 最有价值。\"\n      - \"独立 proxy 验证图：entity count vs SJ ρ 的单调递减趋势，避免 circularity。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Inverted-U pattern 在独立 proxy 验证下成立（用 entity count 替代 F1 分层），\n      排除了 Dream 中 flagged 的 overclaiming 风险。关键 takeaway：self-consistency\n      最有价值的区间是 model 的 \"uncertainty region\"——既不是 knowledge gap（一致地错）\n      也不是 mastery（一致地对），而是 model 有部分能力但不确定的 instance。\n      这为 practical deployment 提供了指导：SJ 在 model 接近 capability frontier 的任务上最有用。\n\n  - name: selection_curves\n    plan_id: exp-010\n    description: >\n      Best-of-N selection curves for N=1,2,4,8,16，所有信号，line plot 可视化。\n    expected_results:\n      scierc_ner_sj_f1_n1: 0.628\n      scierc_ner_sj_f1_n2: 0.660\n      scierc_ner_sj_f1_n4: 0.685\n      scierc_ner_sj_f1_n8: 0.698\n      scierc_ner_sj_f1_n16: 0.712\n      scierc_ner_logprob_f1_n1: 0.628\n      scierc_ner_logprob_f1_n2: 0.648\n      scierc_ner_logprob_f1_n4: 0.668\n      scierc_ner_logprob_f1_n8: 0.680\n      scierc_ner_logprob_f1_n16: 0.687\n      scierc_ner_oracle_f1_n2: 0.680\n      scierc_ner_oracle_f1_n4: 0.728\n      scierc_ner_oracle_f1_n8: 0.759\n      scierc_ner_oracle_f1_n16: 0.797\n      gap_sj_logprob_n2: 1.2\n      gap_sj_logprob_n4: 1.7\n      gap_sj_logprob_n8: 1.8\n      gap_sj_logprob_n16: 2.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      Selection curves 展示 SJ 在所有 N 值上都是最佳选择信号，且 SJ-logprob gap 随 N 递增：\n      - N=2：gap 仅 1.2pp（两个 sample 时 SJ 的 pairwise comparison 退化为单次比较，\n        与 logprob 的差别不大）。\n      - N=16：gap 扩大到 2.5pp（SJ 的 set-level comparison 充分利用了 120 pairwise comparisons）。\n      这个 \"gap widening\" pattern 是 SJ 的核心卖点：投入更多推理预算时，SJ 的边际回报更高。\n      Logprob 的曲线也上升但速率更慢，因为 per-sample logprob 不从更多 sample 中获得\n      额外信息（每个 sample 的 logprob 是独立的，averaging 只是更稳定的估计）。\n      而 SJ 的 signal 本身随 N 增加变得 qualitatively richer（更多 pairwise overlap 信息）。\n      Oracle F1 从 N=2 的 0.680 增至 N=16 的 0.797，展示 headroom 的扩大。\n      SJ 的 headroom utilization（(SJ_F1 - random_F1) / (oracle_F1 - random_F1)）\n      在 N=16 时约 35%，是所有信号中最高的。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Selection curve data (SciERC NER)\"\n        columns: [N, Random_F1, Logprob_F1, FK_F1, SJ_F1, Oracle_F1, SJ-Logprob]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 0.628, 0.628, 0.628, 0.628, 0.628, 0.0]\n          - [2, 0.640, 0.648, 0.651, 0.660, 0.680, +1.2]\n          - [4, 0.652, 0.668, 0.674, 0.685, 0.728, +1.7]\n          - [8, 0.660, 0.680, 0.689, 0.698, 0.759, +1.8]\n          - [16, 0.668, 0.687, 0.698, 0.712, 0.797, +2.5]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot (主图): x=N (log scale), y=F1, 6 条线 (random, logprob, EM, FK, SJ, oracle)。SJ 线在所有 N 上最接近 oracle。\"\n      - \"Gap plot (inset): x=N, y=SJ-logprob gap (pp)，单调递增，展示 'more compute → bigger SJ advantage'。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Selection curve 是论文最有说服力的可视化之一。\"SJ-logprob gap widens with N\" 的 pattern\n      直接回答了 cost-benefit 问题：如果用户已经愿意花 Nx 推理成本做 sampling，\n      用 SJ 而非 logprob 做选择只增加 O(N²) 的 CPU 计算（<1% 的推理成本），\n      但额外获得 1.2-2.5pp F1。这是 \"free lunch\" 论点的核心。\n\n  - name: ner_ood_robustness\n    plan_id: exp-011\n    description: >\n      OOD 测试：用 WNUT-17 fine-tuned model 在 CoNLL-2003 test set 上做 NER inference，\n      或反之。测试 SJ 信号在 domain shift 下的鲁棒性。\n    expected_results:\n      ood_greedy_f1: 0.42\n      ood_oracle_f1: 0.58\n      ood_headroom: 0.16\n      ood_sj_rho: 0.33\n      ood_fk_rho: 0.24\n      ood_logprob_rho: 0.21\n      ood_sj_beats_logprob: true\n      ood_sj_minus_logprob: 0.12\n      ood_sj_bestofn_f1: 0.455\n      ood_sj_over_greedy: 3.5\n      n: 1287\n    result_rationale: >\n      OOD 下 greedy F1 大幅下降（从 in-domain 的 ~0.55-0.72 降至 ~0.42），\n      反映 domain shift 导致 model 能力退化。\n      SJ ρ=0.33 也低于 in-domain（0.37-0.42），但 SJ 仍是最佳信号且仍显著优于 logprob（Δ=0.12）。\n      这一结果有重要的实用意义：在 real-world 部署中，model 经常面对 distribution shift，\n      此时 logprob 因为 model miscalibration（在 OOD data 上 overconfident）而特别不可靠，\n      而 SJ 因为直接度量 output 间的 structural agreement 而更鲁棒——\n      如果 model 在 OOD instance 上不确定，它的 samples 自然会不一致，SJ 会低；\n      如果它碰巧在某个 OOD instance 上仍然一致地正确，SJ 会高。\n      这种 \"behavior-based\" vs \"probability-based\" 的差异在 OOD 下尤为突出。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: In-domain vs OOD signal comparison\"\n        columns: [Setting, Greedy_F1, SJ_rho, FK_rho, Logprob_rho, SJ-Logprob]\n        rows:\n          - [In-domain (WNUT), 0.541, 0.37, 0.28, 0.22, +0.15]\n          - [OOD (WNUT→CoNLL), 0.42, 0.33, 0.24, 0.21, +0.12]\n          - [Delta, -0.121, -0.04, -0.04, -0.01, -0.03]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"In-domain vs OOD bar chart: 展示所有信号在两种 setting 下的 ρ，SJ 的退化幅度最小（-0.04 vs logprob 的 -0.01，但 SJ 的绝对水平始终更高）。\"\n    analysis: >\n      OOD 结果是 appendix material 而非 main body，但为 robustness 提供了额外支撑。\n      SJ 在 OOD 下的优势（+0.12 over logprob）甚至比 logprob 自身的 in-domain 值（0.22）的\n      一半还多，说明在实际部署场景中 SJ 的价值更大。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"72634f08-10d3-4aa1-9d4e-f87016e5fcde","total_cost_usd":0.8613299999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14366,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":30246,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14366,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":30246,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14366,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14366},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":9327,"outputTokens":27,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.009462,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":30246,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":14366,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.851868,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"18fd1a6d-75be-45a1-99ae-7ae0c80ee2df"}
